{"parentUuid":"52ea2bde-4d1b-4a83-9adf-04c5ad051bfe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgntMvAL5iV4Awo7yHtMU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Yes, `lift_v1` and `objects-v1` are the results from Valmet's scene, and they still work.** They came from the damaged cleaned scene, so I started the re-run to see whether undamaged renders give better objects. It may not be worth switching.\n\n**The existing results are usable as they are:**\n- **On the original scene:** object boxes are in scene coordinates, so they should line up with the uncleaned original. You can show the good scene with the current objects. Only `splat_labels.npy` is tied to the cleaned file's order, so anything per-splat (pulling objects apart, cutting them out) would need remapping, which should be straightforward.\n- **Labels and mapping:** they already have 362 AI-reviewed labels, and Eduard's mapping of all 30 Excel records.\n\n**The re-run could only help in these ways:**\n- Masks made from renders without black holes, possibly with better outlines and more of the scene covered (only 26% of splats are in objects today).\n- A cleaner floor map.\n\n**It would cost:**\n- New object IDs, so Eduard's mapping has to be redone.\n- The AI review, which doesn't carry over, so labels start from Qwen alone until I redo it or transfer it by position.\n\n**My recommendation:** keep `objects-v1` as the demo set for now and leave Eduard's work alone. The re-run costs little more GPU time and is already running in separate folders, so I'd let it finish. I'd only switch if it's clearly better, for example much higher object coverage or visibly better outlines on the pumps, and otherwise drop it.\n\nShould I let it finish on those terms, or cancel it now and put the time into drawing routes in the viewer and relabelling from real frames?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1110,"cache_read_input_tokens":304952,"output_tokens":801,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":245},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1110,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":801,"cache_read_input_tokens":304952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1110},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d4d6591a-3090-49a6-9100-d0696b58a851","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgntMunGYXMqgLoxiQvcg","requestRef":"2a2ccdf5-8720-427e-9ff3-5136acd5f6e1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"662c1cad-ba9d-4e99-aead-06853f10ee16","timestamp":"2026-11-07T03:50:17.446Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/keep-faint-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
