{"parentUuid":"56ae71ab-425c-49fc-bafd-91ceb33dbbb9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgntcYy3KWyzpS2KhbRDf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Let the re-run finish, since it needs no attention from me, and don't wait on it.** The biggest gains now are elsewhere, so I'd work in this order:\n\n1. **Fix what's visibly wrong in the demo (about 30 minutes):**\n   - Make the viewer default to Valmet's uncleaned scene, on the current `objects-v1` objects.\n   - Build a new light version from the original for the tablet, because the current ones come from the damaged scene.\n   - Remap `splat_labels.npy` so per-splat features work on the original.\n   - Open the PR for the cleaning fix.\n2. **Draw routes in the viewer, once Benjamin confirms he isn't already on it:** this is the biggest visible gap, and navigation is 25% of the score. It would show the route line, walk along it, and end looking at the pump.\n3. **Choose P-005 on Valmet's scene:** check `obj-0046` by eye, and see whether the two inline pumps are in this scene too. Then get a person to confirm it.\n4. **Rehearse the full flow on the 5090 and tablet:** question, diagnosis, route, arrival, all offline.\n5. **Relabel from real video frames:** this is the best extraction gain (30% of the score), but it comes after a working demo.\n\n**When the re-run finishes:** I'd spend 5 minutes comparing object coverage and the pump outlines. If it isn't clearly better, I'll drop it, so Eduard's mapping stays as it is.\n\n**What I'd stop:** all further work on our own splat, except reusing its video frames for labels.\n\n**You'd need to:** tell Benjamin and Eduard about the cleaning bug and ask Benjamin about route drawing. If you say go, I'll start on step 1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":831,"cache_read_input_tokens":306062,"output_tokens"