\napp/nav/check.py:120:        walked = args.scene / \"walked.npy\"\napp/nav/check.py:121:        start = [float(v) for v in np.load(walked)[0]] if walked.exists() else scene[\"start\"]\napp/copilot/mapping.py:5:Reads `assets_viewer.json`, and uses `nav_grid.npz`, plus the scene's `start` or `walked.npy`.\napp/copilot/mapping.py:7:`mapping.json` and `assets_mapped.json`, the same objects with `mapping` filled in, for the API\napp/copilot/mapping.py:145:    grid_file, walked_file = args.scene / \"nav_grid.npz\", args.scene / \"walked.npy\"\napp/copilot/mapping.py:146:    if grid_file.exists() and (walked_file.exists() or scene.get(\"start\")):\napp/copilot/mapping.py:152:        first = np.load(walked_file)[0] if walked_file.exists() else scene[\"start\"]\napp/copilot/mapping.py:175:    (args.scene / \"assets_mapped.json\").write_text(json.dumps(scene))\ntrain:   ## train a model\n\tuv run python -m app.train\ntb:      ## training graphs at http://localhost:6006\n\tuv run tensorboard --logdir runs","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"373f0212-811d-46e2-bce8-9150bc1c9914","timestamp":"2026-11-07T04:08:39.685Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"10:These links are procedural, not real identities, and are marked that way. Each record goes to one\n11:object. Links already in the file, such as the hand-picked target, are kept. Healthy records go\n113:                    \"method\": \"procedural_class\" if fit == 0 else \"procedural_similar_class\",\n114:                    \"confidence\": EXACT_CONFIDENCE if fit == 0 else SIMILAR_CONFIDENCE,\napp/nav/check.py:93:    parser.add_argument(\"--target\", default=\"P-005\")\ndocs/PLAN.md:14:5. **Reach the fault (`P-005`):** the copilot explains it, cites evidence, and suggests safe checks.\ndocs/PLAN.md:56:2. Write `mapping.json`: match objects to records by class, with `P-005` as the faulty target.\ndocs/PLAN.md:57:3. Pick a local LLM such as Qwen. Build the copilot tools and the `P-005` diagnosis with checked\ndocs/PLAN.md:120:> **Operator:*