{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","id":"7d2c1105-f3a1-4e5d-9f09-460b3d5bf94c","timestamp":"2026-11-07T04:48:12.910Z","version":"2.1.319","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"588ed1bb5cde13c6dac969a3082db367af247bea954d4545a2562540030824a9","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"bd5bedf3-4cb1-4217-81fa-d27c3b8219e2","keep":313,"tail":["985a8cec677eb3d32f72177a5c0c8fd26b3c4afff0c1b4247c1ac4d1dc045553","ac988271a28983c33c66c66662a8fe647548151ad3c3b306fa167bc539a78ffb"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",314,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"d30ddbdea4fa9f298841c1cfc45a29e01ec7da1f28202bbf6ce1f1aaffdc4643"}
{"parentUuid":"206d0e25-d616-4e3e-a03f-30d8a86941fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnxnqsXA1dHGky9XqQ53","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**There's no Qwen or any other language model in the copilot yet.** Qwen currently only labels objects. The copilot is fixed code, with templates filling in Excel data, so it can't handle a free-form question beyond spotting keywords. It reads as canned, which matters because AI diagnostics are 20% of the score and `docs/PLAN.md` calls for a local LLM.\n\nWhat exists is a good base for one: tools that fetch facts with IDs, code-calculated trends, a citation checker and safety guardrails. The plan's design fits on top of that.\n\n**What I'd build, keeping to the plan's rule that the LLM explains facts but doesn't produce them:**\n1. **Guardrails first:** unsafe requests are refused before the model sees them, as now.\n2. **Fetch the facts in code:** status, events, trends, maintenance and documents, each with its ID.\n3. **Qwen writes the answer** from only those facts, in plain language, citing IDs.\n4. **Check the result in code:** the citation checker rejects any ID that wasn't supplied. I'd add a check that every number in the answer appears in the facts.\n5. **Fall back to today's template answer** if the check fails, the model times out or it isn't loaded. The demo can't then break because of the model, and the screen would say which kind of answer it is.\n\n**Why this is worth doing:** follow-ups like \"why would falling flow point to fouling?\" or \"what happened last time?\" would get a real answer, grounded in the records.\n\n**The risks:**\n- **Untested for this job:** I've only benchmarked Qwen3.5-4B on image labels, not on writing from facts. It may invent causes or misstate trends, which is why the checks and fallback matter.\n- **Speed:** it took about 1.2 s per object for labels, but a written answer will take longer. I'd measure it on Roihu's L40, which only roughly predicts the 5090.\n- **Memory:** it used about 10 GB of VRAM alongside the splat viewer on the same 5090. That looks workable, but I can't confirm it until it runs there.\n- **Offline:** the weights must be downloaded ahead of time, and the copilot's dependencies added in their own small PR, as `AGENTS.md` requires.\n\n**The test before trusting it:** about 20 questions on P-005 and other assets, including trick ones (unknown tags, unsafe requests, asking it to guess), checked for invented facts. It only goes in if the checks hold, and the results go in `docs/RESULTS.md`.\n\nI'd start on this now, with the template answer staying as the safe default until the test passes. It's separate from PR #10, but builds on it, so PR #10 should merge first. Should I merge PR #10 and go ahead?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":448857,"output_tokens":892,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":892,"cache_read_input_tokens":448857,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cd4270c1-19fc-4273-a911-d576848a366a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgnxnq4A3jhQYxUw81NuH","requestRef":"7d2c1105-f3a1-4e5d-9f09-460b3d5bf94c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4449c08-a40b-469e-9e6e-1db37c069dc7","timestamp":"2026-11-07T04:48:23.707Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium"