{"parentUuid":"a893ea51-ccd3-4b12-82a8-e4c4e3ae1f52","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgnz1fSwaTGW7EpdwhqRG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vw3Ahpu2CRRXhS7rkwJQMD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='docs/RESULTS.md'; t=open(p).read().rstrip('\\n')\nt+='''\n| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Copilot with a local model, 20 fixed questions, one pass | Excel pack, `lift_v3` objects | Qwen3.5-9B against 4B, facts fetched by code, citations, IDs and numbers checked by code | 9B: 20 of 20 as expected, 14 model answers, 6 refused or template, 3.6 s mean, 6.5 s worst. 4B: 13 of 20 and called health 44 \"high\". Read by hand, 9B blends model confidence 0.91 with the object mapping in one answer, and its causes can be vague. Checks can't catch true facts joined wrongly | About 3 s per answer | 9B 19.5 GB, 4B 9.6 GB VRAM | Roihu L40 |\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\np='handoffs/viktortrilar.md'; t=open(p).read()\nt=re.sub(r\"\\*\\*Verified:\\*\\*.*\\n\",\"**Verified:** lint; all tests with a fake model. Real model: 9B met 20 of 20 on 20 questions, 14 model answers, 3.6 s mean, 19.5 GB VRAM, on Roihu L40. Read by hand, it blends model confidence with the mapping in one answer. P-005 has only pressure and flow data, and nothing links it to M-005\\n\",t)\nt=re.sub(r\"\\*\\*Next:\\*\\*.*\\n\",\"**Next:** merge PR #11, then this PR. On the 5090: `make model`, rehearse offline, and measure memory alongside the viewer. Model answers not yet seen in the viewer\\n\",t)\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\ngit add docs/RESULTS.md handoffs/viktortrilar.md; git commit -qm \"Record the copilot model results\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git fetch -q origin; git merge origin/main --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; make lint 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; git push -q -u git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/copilot-llm 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; gh pr create --head viktor/copilot-llm --base main --title \"Let local Qwen word copilot answers, with code checking the facts\" --body \"$(cat <<'BODY'\n## Changes\n- `app/copilot/llm.py`: code fetches facts and refuses unsafe requests first. Qwen only words the answer. Code then checks its citations, IDs, numbers, and safety.\n- Any failed check, slow reply, or missing model leaves the template answer. The reply and viewer say which kind it is.\n- When the asset record and work orders disagree on the last service, code states it. A model asked to report this merged them into one wrong event.\n- `make model` downloads the weights once, and `make api` uses them if present. Without them, nothing changes.\n- `scripts/eval_copilot.py`: 20 fixed questions, saving every answer.\n\n## Verified\nOn Roihu's L40, Qwen3.5-9B met 20 of 20 expectations: 14 model answers, 3.6 s mean, 19.5 GB VRAM. Unit tests use a fake model.\n\n**Not tested:** the 5090, memory alongside the viewer, `make model`'s download, and model answers in the browser.\n\n**Known limits:** one answer blends model confidence with the object mapping. Checks catch invented IDs and numbers, but not true facts joined wrongly.\n\nNeeds #11 first, for transformers 5.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nBODY\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; sleep 25; gh pr checks 11 2>&1 | cut -c1-30 | head -2; gh pr checks 12 2>&1 | cut -c1-30 | head -2","description":"Record results, update the handoff, push and open the PR","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2314,"cache_read_input_tokens":508062,"output_tokens":1745,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":180},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2314,"ephemeral_5m_inpu