 origin; git merge origin/main --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; make lint 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; git push -q -u git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/copilot-llm 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; gh pr create --head viktor/copilot-llm --base main --title \"Let local Qwen word copilot answers, with code checking the facts\" --body \"$(cat <<'BODY'\n## Changes\n- `app/copilot/llm.py`: code fetches facts and refuses unsafe requests first. Qwen only words the answer. Code then checks its citations, IDs, numbers, and safety.\n- Any failed check, slow reply, or missing model leaves the template answer. The reply and viewer say which kind it is.\n- When the asset record and work orders disagree on the last service, code states it. A model asked to report this merged them into one wrong event.\n- `make model` downloads the weights once, and `make api` uses them if present. Without them, nothing changes.\n- `scripts/eval_copilot.py`: 20 fixed questions, saving every answer.\n\n## Verified\nOn Roihu's L40, Qwen3.5-9B met 20 of 20 expectations: 14 model answers, 3.6 s mean, 19.5 GB VRAM. Unit tests use a fake model.\n\n**Not tested:** the 5090, memory alongside the viewer, `make model`'s download, and model answers in the browser.\n\n**Known limits:** one answer blends model confidence with the object mapping. Checks catch invented IDs and numbers, but not true facts joined wrongly.\n\nNeeds #11 first, for transformers 5.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nBODY\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; sleep 25; gh pr checks 11 2>&1 | cut -c1-30 | head -2; gh pr checks 12 2>&1 | cut -c1-30 | head -2","description":"Record results, update the handoff, push and open the PR","timeout":120000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1c721f36-0362-4e64-bf38-83c188172b9e","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgnz1f8M3L9ey4GMDeSXw","requestRef":"56630db2-6941-4724-89b1-085ec6230898","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assist