{"parentUuid":"f33df23a-0bc6-46d2-83d5-2bdda7703e9e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"77bd0677-a2be-4bec-b1a4-6a9ce32105f1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xrgz81ZEhHLnHE3kwwFPmY","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/PLAN.md:3:We're building a tablet-friendly web demo of a navigable digital twin of a plant room, running entirely\ndocs/PLAN.md:30:| **Benjamin** | Web viewer, tablet, demo video, slides | `web/`, `docs/` | 10% + 25% display |\ndocs/PLAN.md:62:1. Test whether a real tablet can show the splat in Viser. Try a reduced scene if it struggles. Also\ndocs/PLAN.md:80:Tablet viewer ⇄ Backend API ⇄ routing, device data, change log, local AI copilot\ndocs/PLAN.md:104:1. **Open (Benjamin):** load the scene, reduced if the tablet needs it, plus `GET /api/assets`.\ndocs/PLAN.md:116:Question → LLM picks tools → code returns facts with IDs → LLM answers → code checks citations → tablet\ndocs/PLAN.md:221:1. See it: manual \"Add obstacle\" on the tablet (demo), a short clip (future), or cameras (future).\ndocs/PLAN.md:227:1. **Manually on the tablet:** \"Add obstacle\" or \"Removed\". This is what we demo.\ndocs/PLAN.md:238:- **Tablet connection:** bring our own router, and don't rely on venue Wi-Fi.\ndocs/PLAN.md:252:local Wi-Fi, and recent tablets.\ndocs/PLAN.md:261:| 6. Use | Alarm opens on a tablet, follow the route, ask the copilot, draft a work order | Technician |\ndocs/PLAN.md:271:| Object identity | Rule-based mapping | Confirmed by engineers, with QR or NFC tags where needed |\ndocs/PLAN.md:272:| Technician position | Simulated from a chosen start | QR checkpoints or AR tracking |\ndocs/CHALLENGE.md:10:**Valmet's wider vision:** their representative described a person using this on a tablet to see\ndocs/CHALLENGE.md:12:mobile or Android frontend. So we build a browser app that works on a tablet, not a native app.\ndocs/CHALLENGE.md:41:- Repo with a concise README and setup instructions\ndocs/CHALLENGE.md:56:The pack is synthetic. Its `Scene_Anchors` coordinates are placeholders, not real scene positions.\n// Phone mode: turn the phone to look around, walk to move, or use the on-screen joystick.\n// Works in any phone browser (iPhone Safari too). Sensors need HTTPS: run `make web HTTPS=1`.\n//\n// Walking is estimated by counting steps, so it only moves forward and drifts over longer walks.\n// Press Start to put the camera back at the start and make the phone's current facing \"forward\".\nimport * as THREE from \"three\";\n\nconst STEP_LENGTH = 0.7; // metres per detected step\nconst WALK_SPEED = 1.4; // metres per second, to glide each step instead of jumping\nconst JOYSTICK_SPEED = 1.5; // metres per second at full deflection\nconst GRAVITY = 9.81;\nconst STEP_HIGH = 1.2; // a step peaks this far above gravity (m/s^2)...\nconst STEP_LOW = 0.3; // ...and must fall back below this before the next one counts\nconst STEP_MIN_MS = 300; // fastest step rate we accept\n\nconst Y = new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0);\n4:// Walking is estimated by counting steps, so it only moves forward and drifts over longer walks.\n8:const STEP_LENGTH = 0.7; // metres per detected step\n9:const WALK_SPEED = 1.4; // metres per second, to glide each step instead of jumping\n12:const STEP_HIGH = 1.2; // a step peaks this far above gravity (m/s^2)...\n14:const STEP_MIN_MS = 300; // fastest step rate we accept\n47:  let steps = 0;\n48:  let pending = 0; // metres still to glide from detected steps\n66:      steps++;\n78:    for (const Sensor of [window.DeviceOrientationEvent, window.DeviceMotionEvent]) {\n86:    window.addEventListener(\"deviceorientation\", onOrientation);\n82:    scene_anchor_id: str = \"\"\n83:    qr_id: str = \"\"\n84:    nfc_id: str = \"\"\n230:                scene_anchor_id=_safe_str(r.get(\"scene_anchor_id\")),","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ba244c5f-1172-44fa-bea8-d8c6043d57fe","timestamp":"2026-11-07T07:09:29.884Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/PLAN.md:3:We're building a tablet-friendly 