{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","id":"e101e73a-9d0e-46ef-afe7-22159c3222ef","timestamp":"2026-11-07T07:09:29.957Z","version":"2.1.319","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"588ed1bb5cde13c6dac969a3082db367af247bea954d4545a2562540030824a9","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"6c9421ef-eb31-4062-b97c-2c5490727547","keep":380,"tail":["e57a55537a2f41271cfa339b9c57397daafaa5bd7b1bc7412c6404bf7d45ec7e","ec2749d5b36978082d2e766d02da668871a3b14b8d291e40892c70dd7d2ae4d9"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",381,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"4432bf91fd5d4cbcd61383ec632c2b554c88f4de587ced4a819e5ba72467941a"}
{"parentUuid":"ba244c5f-1172-44fa-bea8-d8c6043d57fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo9Zm4xvwtRQuhtqgkRE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Human navigation works on the digital twin today, but the system doesn't know where the real person is standing.** Voice mode is doable offline, and would take me about a few hours to a working version. That's my estimate, as none of it is built.\n\n## Human navigation today\n| Part | Status |\n|---|---|\n| **Body size** | Routes are planned for a 0.6 m wide person, staying clear of obstacles and movable objects |\n| **Route line** | Drawn on the floor in the viewer |\n| **Walk route** | The virtual camera walks at 1.2 m/s and ends about 2 m back, looking at the target |\n| **Refusals** | If no route exists, it says why, such as \"closest reachable floor is 2.9 m away\" |\n| **Phone mode (Benjamin's)** | Turning the tablet turns the view, and steps are counted as 0.7 m each, or you can use a joystick |\n\n**The limits for a real person walking the room:**\n- **Position is only an estimate.** It starts from a chosen point, and step counting drifts over longer walks. `docs/PLAN.md` already lists this as a future item (\"QR checkpoints or AR tracking\").\n- **There are no spoken or written directions.** You get a line, not \"turn left in 3 m\".\n- **Re-planning starts from the camera,** so it's only as accurate as that position.\n\n**What I'd add, cheapest first:**\n1. **Written directions from the route,** like \"walk 2 m, turn right, the pump is ahead\". It's a small job, and voice mode needs it anyway.\n2. **QR checkpoints:** scan a printed code to correct your position. The Excel pack has QR IDs, but its `Scene_Anchors` coordinates are placeholders, so we'd have to place the codes ourselves. Good for explaining the idea, less useful for a stage demo.\n3. **Matching camera images to the scene:** the real answer, but too risky for this deadline, as my frame-alignment failure showed. I'd mention it as future work.\n\nFor the demo, I'd keep the position simulated and say so plainly. `docs/PLAN.md` already plans it that way.\n\n## How voice mode would work\nEverything has to run locally, which rules out the browser's built-in speech recognition, since Chrome's version sends audio to a cloud service.\n\n**Push to talk → record on tablet → speech-to-text on the 5090 (e.g. Whisper) → same copilot and safety checks → text-to-speech on the 5090 (e.g. Piper) → play on tablet**\n\n- **Speed:** I'd guess 5–6 seconds per reply, of which the copilot takes about 3.6 s. It needs measuring.\n- **Memory:** a small Whisper model should only add 1–2 GB on top of Qwen's 19.5 GB.\n- **HTTPS is required for the mic.** `make web HTTPS=1` already does this, and the viewer's server already forwards the API calls.\n- **Show what it heard.** This matters in a noisy plant, because mishearing a tag could send someone to the wrong machine. Safety checks run on the transcribed text, so a misheard \"stop the pump\" still gets refused.\n- **Spoken answers need to be short.** Read out the answer only, and leave sources and evidence on screen.\n- **Voice commands** could drive the viewer too: \"take me to P-005\" draws the route and reads the directions.\n\n## What I recommend\nNeither the brief notes nor the plan mention voice, so it wouldn't directly score, as far as I can see. It would make a strong demo moment though, hands-free for someone in gloves, and it would count towards the demo's 10% and the copilot's impression.\n\nThe order I'd go in:\n1. Merge #11 and #12, then do the offline rehearsal on the 5090. Don't add features before that has worked once.\n2. Add written directions.\n3. Add voice with a typed fallback, so a failed mic can't sink the demo.\n\nShould I merge and start on the directions now, or do you want voice first?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2407,"cache_read_input_tokens":514754,"output_tokens":1307,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2407,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1307,"cache_read_input_tokens":514754,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2407},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ded3d3ef-c3cb-49c8-8915-8ad0688128ed","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgo9ZkZx7kbnyAHkCMh3d","requestRef":"e101e73a-9d0e-46ef-afe7-22159c3222ef","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"74f54186-2fe8-42e9-acff-67d82cbd08db","timestamp":"2026-11-07T07:09:44.709Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/copilot-llm","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
