{"parentUuid":"bc0813d6-2b71-4460-8277-f4054bcd4f2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoCy3USRzDYb8EBVGg6c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019w43ZmyWFH4AxXYswmL2gP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='Makefile'; t=open(p).read()\nt=t.replace(\"PIECES_OBJECTS ?= obj-0067 obj-0008\",\"PIECES_OBJECTS ?= obj-0067\")\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\np='docs/RESULTS.md'; t=open(p).read().rstrip('\\n')\nt=re.sub(r\"\\| 2026-11-07 \\| Viktor \\| Moving real objects.*\\n?\",\"\",t).rstrip('\\n')\nt+='''\n| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Moving real objects (`app/scene/split_movable.py`) | Uncleaned `Equipment Room.ply` | Everything in the box down to the floor, then real floor splats copied from clear floor under it | Roll cage `obj-0067` moves cleanly, floor behind looks whole by eye. Real mouse drag to (-1.46, -1.75): route to `obj-0049` from 4.31 to 5.56 m, undo restores it. Chair `obj-0008` not used by default: its low base looks thinner even in place. The patch isn't scanned: `patches.json` records where | | | Roihu L40, headless browser |\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\np='handoffs/viktortrilar.md'; t=open(p).read()\nt=re.sub(r\"\\*\\*Verified:\\*\\*.*\\n\",\"**Verified:** lint; all tests. Browser: real drag, add, save, re-route, undo (before the floor patch). Renders: roll cage moves cleanly with a whole-looking floor; chair's base looks thin, so it's off by default. Selection median overlap 0.35 against known boxes. Qwen 9B sensible on 6 crops. Not tested: 5090, tablet, full scene in the viewer\\n\",t)\nt=re.sub(r\"\\*\\*Next:\\*\\*.*\\n\",\"**Next:** merge PR #13. Rehearse on the 5090 offline. Mask-based cutting for more objects. Written directions. A person confirms P-005 on obj-0049\\n\",t)\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\nT=\"$S/make_test\"; rm -rf \"$S/cut_test\"; uv run --no-sync --with numpy python -m app.scene.split_movable \"$T/light_400k.ply\" \"$T/assets_viewer.json\" \"$S/cut_test\" --objects obj-0067 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-260; uv run --no-sync ruff format app tests web/serve.py 2>&1 | tail -1; make lint 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; uv run --no-project --with numpy --with scipy --with pandas --with openpyxl --with pytest --with fastapi --with httpx --with pillow --with 'psycopg[binary]' pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; git add -A app tests web Makefile docs/RESULTS.md handoffs/viktortrilar.md; git status --short | grep -v \"^[AMD] \" | head -3; git commit -qm \"Keep low object parts with their object, and default to the roll cage\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git fetch -q origin; git merge origin/main --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/moving-splats 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-40; gh pr edit 13 --title \"Move real objects when dragged, patch the floor, and let operators add objects\" --body \"$(cat <<'BODY'\n## Changes\n- **Moving real objects:** `make pieces` cuts objects out of a scene, down to the floor. The viewer moves the real splats with the drag. Re-plans keep the route's start.\n- **Floor patch:** the floor under a cut object is replaced with real floor splats copied from a clear spot, recorded in `patches.json`. This is estimated, not scanned, and only the viewer uses it.\n- **Adding objects:** **Add object** in the viewer. Drag a box or tap, and code measures it from the splats. A vision model suggests the label, code sets mobility by rule, and the operator confirms before saving. New objects block routes, survive a restart, and never get an identity link.\n\n## Verified\nLint and tests. Headless browser: real mouse drag bends the route from 4.31 to 5.56 m, add, save and re-route work, and undo restores both. These ran before the floor patch. Renders with the patch look clean for the roll cage. Selection: median overlap 0.35 with known boxes, so it's a rough box with Bigger and Smaller buttons. Qwen 9B gave sensible labels on 6 crops.\n\n**Not tested:** the 5090, a tablet, the full scene in the viewer, or a real model's suggestion through the browser.\n\n**Limits:** only the roll cage moves as real splats by default, and anything else in its box moves too. The chair's low base looks thin, so it's off by default.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nBODY\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; sleep 20; gh pr checks 13 2>&1 | cut -c1-30 | head -1","description":"Set the default, run all tests, push and update the PR","timeout":150000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1288,"cache_read_input_tokens":629790,"output_tokens":2332,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":340},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1288,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2332,"cache_read_input_tokens":629790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1288},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15700,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019w43ZmyWFH4AxXYswmL2gP":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='Makefile'; t=open(p).read()\nt=t.replace(\"PIECES_OBJECTS ?= obj-0067 obj-0008\",\"PIECES_OBJECTS ?= obj-0067\")\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\np='docs/RESULTS.md'; t=open(p).read().rstrip('\\n')\nt=re.sub(r\"\\| 2026-11-07 \\| Viktor \