{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","prNumber":13,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/13","prRepository":"Sairanyx/Newbies","timestamp":"2026-11-07T07:55:37.681Z"}
{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01W2z6u48mE7ruGEe22DNPVT","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"eb1ff47f-cfbf-49b1-a15e-4ca693f2c22a","ownerOrganizationUuid":"af454b37-7570-4ffb-9890-36a908611f8b"}
{"parentUuid":"14701df0-1401-4ce2-b47e-8d26c4cf6beb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoD5f6Eg6XkGXpMFsz8j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Both features are done and in [PR #13](https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/13), but they aren't merged yet.** All tests pass (179, with 2 skipped), and CI passes.\n\n## Adding missed objects\nClick **Add object** in the viewer, then drag a box or tap the object:\n\n1. **Code measures it** from the splats in your selection and shows an orange box, with **Bigger** and **Smaller** buttons to adjust it.\n2. **The vision model suggests a label** from what's on screen. It can also pick up text it can read, and if that matches a known tag, it shows \"may be P-005: not linked\".\n3. **Code sets mobility by rule** from the label, not from the model.\n4. **You confirm or change it, then save.** The generated config is viewable on the panel.\n\nSaved objects block routes straight away, are designed to survive a restart (I tested that with a stand-in database, not the real one), and can be undone. They're marked \"new, unconfirmed\", and code won't accept an identity link or status from this flow, in keeping with never inventing identity.\n\n**How well it works:**\n- **Selection is rough.** Against known objects, median overlap is 0.35: 64% of selections reach 0.3 or more, 16% reach 0.5 or more, and 1% found nothing. Known boxes are imperfect too, but from high angles or in clutter the box can come out too large. It warns when the box overlaps existing objects.\n- **Qwen's labels look good on a small test.** It got the chair, cart, roll cage, washing machine and bucket right on 5 crops. On a wide view with no single object, it still said \"chair\" instead of \"unknown\", which is why confirming matters.\n\nWithout the model, you just pick the label yourself.\n\n## The floor behind moved objects\nI went with a simpler method than inpainting: **a 3D clone stamp that copies real floor splats from a clear spot nearby.** It needs no new model, and it looks right from every angle.\n\n- **Roll cage:** the dark patch is gone, and the floor behind looks whole by eye.\n- **Chair:** not good enough yet. Its star base is so low it reads as floor. My fix makes the base move with it, but it looks thin even before moving, so **I turned the chair off by default.**\n- **Disclosure:** the patch is estimated, not scanned. `patches.json` records where, and the viewer can't yet tint it, so it should be mentioned in the technical note. Routing uses the real scan, not the patch.\n\n## Limits\n- **Only the roll cage moves as real splats by default.** Mask-based cutting for more objects isn't built yet.\n- **Tested separately:** the browser test covered dragging, adding and undo, but it ran before the floor patch. The patch was only checked in renders, and Qwen's suggestions only on crops, not through the browser.\n- **Not run at all:** the 5090, a tablet, and the full scene in the viewer. There's now a lot of new code that's never run on real hardware together.\n\n## Next steps\n1. **Merge #13.** Should I?\n2. **Run the rehearsal on the 5090 now, before adding anything else.** Every feature since the last rehearsal plan has added risk, and the deadline may be Sunday 09:00 (still unconfirmed). Valmet's scene, the Qwen model, routes, moving and adding objects all need to run together offline at least once:\n   ```\n   make scene mapping db model pieces\n   make api\n   make web SCENE=data/scene/equipment_room/cut/base.ply ASSETS=data/scene/equipment_room/assets_mapped.json SHAPES=data/scene/equipment_room/shapes.json PIECES=data/scene/equipment_room/cut\n   ```\n   Start `make web` in a second terminal, since `make api` keeps running. `make model` needs internet and about 20 GB, so run it first.\n3. **After that:** mask-based cutting for more objects, written directions, then voice if there's time."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":800,"cache_read_input_tokens":633657,"output_tokens":1300,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":800,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":633657,"cache_creation_input_tokens":800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":800},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f3cbe41d-b643-42eb-90d2-d227b429d2cf","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoD5eiuhs135Q3F42Acd","requestRef":"5bdcbf42-2cd4-41c3-93a9-13b404d04b6e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b95968b8-f411-4060-a879-0e9e691ee493","timestamp":"2026-11-07T07:55:51.342Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/moving-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
