{"parentUuid":"a29083d5-9f0c-4479-9fa1-e125eb861117","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoEpGHMXDTcY3VedMRVc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YG42tmgz3nZg8e9eoW7qEV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='web/main.js'; t=open(p).read()\nt=t.replace('''function name(asset) {\n  return asset.mapping?.tag ?? asset.label;\n}\n''','''// Links made by rule aren't real identities, so they're shown as a question.\nfunction name(asset) {\n  const link = asset.mapping;\n  if (!link) return asset.label;\n  return link.method?.startsWith(\"procedural\") ? `${link.tag}?` : link.tag;\n}\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"name(o.asset) === o.asset.label\" web/main.js | cut -c1-90; sed -i 's/^from app.api.main import create_app/from app.api.main import app as api_app/; s/^c=TestClient(create_app())/c=TestClient(api_app)/' \"$S/api_real.py\"; K=\"$PWD/cert(13).pub\"; R=vtrilar@roihu-cpu-login1.csc.fi; B=/scratch/project_2020113/sinceai; O=(-o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=20 -o \"CertificateFile=$K\"); scp -q \"${O[@]}\" \"$S/api_real.py\" $R:$B/scripts/; ssh \"${O[@]}\" $R \"sbatch $B/scripts/api_real.sbatch 2>&1 | tail -1\"; cat > handoffs/viktortrilar.md <<'EOF'\n# viktortrilar: viktor/moving-splats\n**Goal:** close the limits on moving objects and on testing everything together\n**Done:** app/scene/movable_members.py cuts by masks. Four checked objects move as real splats (roll cage by box; chairs obj-0021, obj-0008 and box obj-0112 by masks), others as outlines. Add object, floor patch, Range limit (at most 15 frames, 8 labels), and a \"?\" on procedural links. members.npz is in Release objects-v2\n**Verified:** lint; tests. Full flow in a headless browser with the template copilot: route, copilot, refusal, drag to 5.56 m, add, undo, no page errors. Real Qwen 9B through the API on Roihu: checked answers in about 3 s, refusal, label suggestion. Full scene loads in the viewer with no errors, at 1 fps in software. By eye, only 3 of 25 high-scoring mask cuts look clean\n**Not tested:** 5090, tablet, real frame rate, model text shown in the browser (compute node login refused the tunnel)\n**Next:** merge PR #13 and rehearse on the 5090. Then a per-scene config and `make pipeline`: the full job is still only in scratch. A second room would prove transfer\n**Blockers:** none. P-005 on obj-0049 is an unconfirmed pick. Cert valid to 2026-11-07 20:41\nEOF\nmake lint 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; uv run --no-project --with numpy --with scipy --with pandas --with openpyxl --with pytest --with fastapi --with httpx --with pillow --with 'psycopg[binary]' pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; git add web handoffs/viktortrilar.md; git commit -qm \"Mark procedural links as uncertain in the viewer\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git fetch -q origin; git merge origin/main --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/moving-splats 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-40; git log --oneline -1 | cut -c1-60","description":"Mark procedural links, measure memory with one model load, test, and push","timeout":150000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2040,"cache_read_input_tokens":691665,"output_tokens":2995,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1144},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2040,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2995,"cache_read_input_tokens":691665,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2040,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens