{"parentUuid":"26167f92-c8ea-4a14-9130-bca7033c6c2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoEwgGBnLt6fxot9NYbo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":697542,"output_tokens":1461,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":72},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":404,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1461,"cache_read_input_tokens":697542,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":404},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7373,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"090d63c4-29c0-4df4-9eea-59d2e89f88c2","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoEwfuN7U77HZqrYY34M","requestRef":"ba61a15b-dc76-4dfb-978d-200fcc31097b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d8c2e464-4ea0-4557-85c3-8cd65ed9d914","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:20:11.373Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/moving-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"d8c2e464-4ea0-4557-85c3-8cd65ed9d914","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoEwgGBnLt6fxot9NYbo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**I've closed most of the limits, and moving objects got a more modest result than the score suggested.** PR #13 is pushed, with CI passing and 182 tests passing (2 skipped), but it isn't merged. What's left mostly needs the real 5090.\n\n## Limits\n| Limit | Result |\n|---|---|\n| **Only one object moved as real splats** | **Four now:** the roll cage, two chairs and a cardboard box, on both the full and light scenes. The others still move as outlines |\n| **Features tested separately** | **Full flow passes in the browser, no page errors:** route, health display, copilot, refusal, drag (4.31 to 5.56 m), add object, undo. This run used template copilot answers |\n| **Real Qwen untested with the API** | **Works:** checked answers in about 3 s, refusals, the service-date note, and a chair labelled at 0.94 confidence from a selection |\n| **Memory on the 5090** | **Should fit:** 19.5 GB with text and image use together on Roihu's GPU. An alarming 38.3 GB reading was my test loading the model twice. Viewer memory still has to share the same card |\n| **Full scene in the viewer** | **Loads with no errors:** all 1,676,481 splats, with and without level of detail. It ran at 1 fps here, but that's software rendering, so it says nothing about the 5090 |\n| **Clutter in the view** | **Added:** at most 15 frames and 8 labels, and a Range button for 2, 3, 5 or 10 m. The fault and your selection always show, then linked equipment, with pipes last |\n\n## Moving objects: the honest number\nMask-based cutting got 25 of 54 objects past a 0.7 match score, but **only 3 of those looked clean by eye**. Objects in piles leave smears, and the see-through roll cage scored just 0.33 with mask cutting while looking best with the box cut. So I hand-picked the four rather than trusting the score. The chair `obj-0008`, with its thin base under the old cut, now uses mask cutting.\n\nSo don't claim \"every object can move\". What's true is that four are checked as real splats, and the rest move as outlines.\n\n## Other fix\nThe viewer was showing \"M-005\" on a washing machine as if it were a fact. Those Excel links are procedural, made by rule, so they now show as \"M-005?\". The panel explains how each was linked.\n\n## Still weak\n- **Selection boxes can be too big:** selecting the chair gave a box about 1.8 m long, for a chair about 0.5 m long, and it flagged 9 overlaps. The label was right, but you may need **Smaller**, which shrinks all sides evenly. A better selection would use SAM on the chosen area.\n- **Model text in the browser panel is untested.** The tunnel to the GPU node was refused, so I tested the viewer and the model separately. The panel code is simple, but check it in the rehearsal.\n- **Only you can test these:** the 5090, a tablet, real frame rate, and offline running.\n- **Another room:** the config file and `make pipeline` aren't built, and the full pipeline job still lives only in my scratch folder.\n\n## Next steps\n1. **Merge #13.** Should I? It also makes `make scene`'s newly uploaded data (`members.npz`) usable by `make pieces`.\n2. **Rehearse on the 5090.** With internet, run `make scene mapping db model pieces`, then go offline:\n   ```\n   make api\n   make web SCENE=data/scene/equipment_room/cut/base.ply ASSETS=data/scene/equipment_room/assets_mapped.json SHAPES=data/scene/equipment_room/shapes.json PIECES=data/scene/equipment_room/cut\n   ```\n   Run them in two terminals, since `make api` keeps running. Then try **Go to P-005**, **Walk route**, **Copilot**, dragging the roll cage, and **Add object**. If you send me what breaks, I'll fix it.\n3. **While you do that,** I can build the per-scene config and `make pipeline`, which only needs Roihu. Do you have a second room's scan, or can someone film one? It's the only way to prove the pipeline transfers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":697542,"output_tokens":1461,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":72},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":404,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1461,"cache_read_input_tokens":697542,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":404},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"090d63c4-29c0-4df4-9eea-59d2e89f88c2","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoEwfuN7U77HZqrYY34M","requestRef":"ba61a15b-dc76-4dfb-978d-200fcc31097b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"7df7b90e-17d7-4adf-81eb-581a88fa3a76","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:20:18.005Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/moving-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
