{"parentUuid":"45b9290c-6a3d-4aef-be18-9e5e521a09c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoFDiVqFKYVSveTMqNFm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GPNsMjm2kqsQjZ4CieLeB8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; sed -n 14,46p docs/CHALLENGE.md | cut -c1-170; sed -n 6,14p docs/RESULTS.md | cut -c1-150; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,numpy as np\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport glob\nP=glob.glob('/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad/obj_v2_pkg/assets_viewer.json')[0]\nA=json.load(open(P))['assets']\nprint(Counter(a['label_grade'] for a in A)); print(Counter(a['label'] for a in A).most_common(10))\nv=np.array([np.prod(np.array(a['bbox_max'])-a['bbox_min']) for a in A]); s=np.array([a['splats'] for a in A]); print('vol<1L',int((v<.001).sum()),'splats<200',int((s<200).sum()),'median vol',round(float(np.median(v)),4))\nprint('pipe count',sum(a['label']=='pipe' for a in A),'with long side>1m',sum(a['label']=='pipe' and max(np.array(a['bbox_max'])-a['bbox_min'])>1 for a in A))\nEOF","description":"Read the brief's success criteria and current object statistics"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1480,"cache_read_input_tokens":697946,"output_tokens":886,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":343},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1480,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":886,"cache_read_input_tokens":697946,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1480},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":4700,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GPNsMjm2kqsQjZ4CieLeB8":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; sed -n 14,46p docs/CHALLENGE.md | cut -c1-170; sed -n 6,14p docs/RESULTS.md | cut -c1-150; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,numpy as np\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport glob\nP=glob.glob('/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad/obj_v2_pkg/assets_viewer.json')[0]\nA=json.load(open(P))['assets']\nprint(Counter(a['label_grade'] for a in A)); print(Counter(a['label'] for a in A).most_common(10))\nv=np.array([np.prod(np.array(a['bbox_max'])-a['bbox_min']) for a in A]); s=np.array([a['splats'] for a in A]); print('vol<1L',int((v<.001).sum()),'splats<200',int((s<200).sum()),'median vol',round(float(np.median(v)),4))\nprint('pipe count',sum(a['label']=='pipe' for a in A),'with long side>1m',sum(a['label']=='pipe' and max(np.array(a['bbox_max'])-a['bbox_min'])>1 for a in A))\nEOF","description":"Read the brief's success criteria and current object statistics"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"019ebd5f-9fac-4c96-9698-2e32e464350c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoFDhoQNQpN93a2KigYG","requestRef":"a50defef-2b3d-4684-8fbb-ec85589df4af","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"23a0c49f-9c1a-4d18-a7d1-04e92f497bdd","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:23:50.204Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/moving-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"23a0c49f-9c1a-4d18-a7d1-04e92f497bdd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"51272068-02bd-4285-b9fd-82e4758896c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GPNsMjm2kqsQjZ4CieLeB8","type":"tool_result","content":"**Extra credit (verbal, from their engineer):** turn the scene into separate objects that can be\nmoved, like `semantic extraction demo 1` (\"Every object, its own asset\": select, move, simulate).\n\n## What to build\nFocus on backend and spatial processing, and keep the UI lightweight.\n\n1. **Extract assets:** detect and put 3D boxes around as many objects as possible in\n   `Industrial Boiler Room.ply`.\n2. **Map metadata:** link extracted assets to the Excel pack. Random or procedural mapping is\n   allowed, with a pre-determined faulty target device.\n3. **Navigate:** a worker or robot follows an automatic, collision-free route on the floor to the\n   faulty device.\n4. **Show nearby assets:** highlight 3D boxes and metadata for assets near the avatar as it moves.\n5. **Diagnose:** on arrival, an AI assistant explains the fault and recommends next steps, grounded\n   in the Excel pack.\n\n## Scoring\n| Weight | Criterion |\n|---|---|\n| 30% | Number and quality of extracted, 3D-framed assets mapped to metadata |\n| 25% | Realistic obstacle-free navigation and proximity display |\n| 20% | AI diagnostics, grounding and explainability |\n| 15% | Backend architecture: structured, automated, modular |\n| 10% | Demo clarity and innovation |\n\n## Submission\n- Working demo, runnable locally or clearly recorded\n- Repo with a concise README and setup instructions\n- 5-8 slides: extraction pipeline, pathfinding, metadata mapping, AI approach\n- Demo video, 5 minutes maximum\n- Brief technical note on models, libraries, and software\n\n## Data\n## Scenes\n| Check | `Equipment Room.ply` | Own splat |\n|---|---|---|\n| Assets framed | Not run | Not built |\n| Junk boxes, out of 30 sampled | Not run | Not built |\n| Route reaches `P-005` candidate without clipping | Not compared on one object | `obj-0048`: 6.8 m at 0.6 m wide, looks clear in 7 rendered views alo\n| Floor area connected at 0.6 m wide (Valmet with movable objects and low clutter left out) | 7.4 m2 | 0.2 m2 without floater removal, 6.6 m2 with it.\n| Held-out views, 40 frames, against real photos. Not a fair test: the frames are from our video, and Valmet's scene is a different capture (a chair, \n| Look from the same viewpoints, on and 0.6 m off our path, both uncleaned, by eye | Near-photographic, complete floor and ceiling. Chosen for the dem\nCounter({'ai_reviewed': 302, 'likely': 68, 'unsure': 38, 'unknown': 32})\n[('pipe', 154), ('object', 109), ('cart', 20), ('electrical cabinet', 19), ('box', 19), ('cable', 17), ('tank', 14), ('valve', 12), ('bag', 11), ('ladder', 9)]\nvol<1L 31 splats<200 139 median vol 0.0153\npipe count 154 with long side>1m 72","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f5c4083b-bd69-4a53-89f4-0742bf8c0600","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:23:50.874Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"**Extra credit (verbal, from their engineer):** turn the scene into separate objects that can be\nmoved, like `semantic extraction demo 1` (\"Every object, its own asset\": select, move, simulate).\n\n## What to build\nFocus on backend and spatial processing, and keep the UI lightweight.\n\n1. **Extract assets:** detect and put 3D boxes around as many objects as possible in\n   `Industrial Boiler Room.ply`.\n2. **Map metadata:** link extracted assets to the Excel pack. Random or procedural mapping is\n   allowed, with a pre-determined faulty target device.\n3. **Navigate:** a worker or robot follows an automatic, collision-free route on the floor to the\n   faulty device.\n4. **Show nearby assets:** highlight 3D boxes and metadata for assets near the avatar as it moves.\n5. **Diagnose:** on arrival, an AI assistant explains the fault and recommends next steps, grounded\n   in the Excel pack.\n\n## Scoring\n| Weight | Criterion |\n|---|---|\n| 30% | Number and quality of extracted, 3D-framed assets mapped to metadata |\n| 25% | Realistic obstacle-free navigation and proximity display |\n| 20% | AI diagnostics, grounding and explainability |\n| 15% | Backend architecture: structured, automated, modular |\n| 10% | Demo clarity and innovation |\n\n## Submission\n- Working demo, runnable locally or clearly recorded\n- Repo with a concise README and setup instructions\n- 5-8 slides: extraction pipeline, pathfinding, metadata mapping, AI approach\n- Demo video, 5 minutes maximum\n- Brief technical note on models, libraries, and software\n\n## Data\n## Scenes\n| Check | `Equipment Room.ply` | Own splat |\n|---|---|---|\n| Assets framed | Not run | Not built |\n| Junk boxes, out of 30 sampled | Not run | Not built |\n| Route reaches `P-005` candidate without clipping | Not compared on one object | `obj-0048`: 6.8 m at 0.6 m wide, looks clear in 7 rendered views alo\n| Floor area connected at 0.6 m wide (Valmet with movable objects and low clutter left out) | 7.4 m2 | 0.2 m2 without floater removal, 6.6 m2 with it.\n| Held-out views, 40 frames, against real photos. Not a fair test: the frames are from our video, and Valmet's scene is a different capture (a chair, \n| Look from the same viewpoints, on and 0.6 m off our path, both uncleaned, by eye | Near-photographic, complete floor and ceiling. Chosen for the dem\nCounter({'ai_reviewed': 302, 'likely': 68, 'unsure': 38, 'unknown': 32})\n[('pipe', 154), ('object', 109), ('cart', 20), ('electrical cabinet', 19), ('box', 19), ('cable', 17), ('tank', 14), ('valve', 12), ('bag', 11), ('ladder', 9)]\nvol<1L 31 splats<200 139 median vol 0.0153\npipe count 154 with long side>1m 72","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"019ebd5f-9fac-4c96-9698-2e32e464350c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","branch":"viktor/moving-splats","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":null,"remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"23a0c49f-9c1a-4d18-a7d1-04e92f497bdd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/moving-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
