{"parentUuid":"f5c4083b-bd69-4a53-89f4-0742bf8c0600","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoFEUfuSvfvr93LA7SJb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1971,"cache_read_input_tokens":699426,"output_tokens":2271,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":856},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1971,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2271,"cache_read_input_tokens":699426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1971},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":18372,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"dcc496a4-82cc-4866-bd5a-9b95e88d82ff","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoFEUEcstuez6sZ5EzP4","requestRef":"3f8f2a9b-8668-47ad-a894-277c1d781ab6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6335da76-2da5-4393-a722-7fd62f7c8af5","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:24:10.071Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/moving-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"6335da76-2da5-4393-a722-7fd62f7c8af5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoFEUfuSvfvr93LA7SJb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The biggest gain isn't raising a number, it's measuring the ones that score the most.** Extraction is 30% of the score, and we've never measured its quality: the \"Assets framed\" and \"Junk boxes\" checks in `docs/RESULTS.md` still say \"Not run\" for this scene. Most of our other label figures are my own AI review, not ground truth.\n\n## Where we stand, by scoring weight\n| Criterion | What we have | What's weak |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Extraction, 30%** | 440 objects framed, 302 AI-reviewed, 68 likely | 109 still show as just \"object\". 139 have under 200 splats, so some are probably fragments. Junk rate unknown |\n| **Metadata mapping** (same 30%) | All 30 Excel records linked | Only 30 of 440 objects, and 29 links are procedural. That's allowed, but P-005's pick is unconfirmed |\n| **Navigation, 25%** | 11.3 m² connected at 0.6 m wide, 384 of 440 reachable, 210 within 0.8 m | Clearance only checked by eye on one walk. Nearby display untested on a real walk |\n| **AI, 20%** | 20 of 20 expectations met, 14 model answers | Small test, and \"passed the checks\" isn't the same as \"correct\" |\n| **Backend, 15%** | 182 tests passing, modular code | No single pipeline command |\n| **Demo, 10%** | Real moving objects, route detour, add object | Not rehearsed, and slides and video unchecked |\n\n## What I'd do, in order\nTimes are my estimates.\n\n**1. Measure extraction precision (about 30 minutes).** Take a random sample of 60 objects, show them on review sheets, and count real, correctly labelled, or junk. That gives one honest number for the slides, like \"x of 60 are real objects\". Ideally a person scores it, otherwise I do and we say so.\n\n**2. Clean up the object list (about 1–2 hours).**\n- Review the 138 objects with no AI-review grade, which should shrink that 109 \"object\" group.\n- Merge fragments into their parent objects, and remove junk, which should raise quality even though the count drops.\n- Group pipe pieces into runs. 154 pipes is a lot of boxes for fewer real pipes, and 72 are over 1 m long.\n\n**3. Frame more real objects (about 1–2 hours, uncertain).** Only about half of the solid splats belong to an object. Run a second pass on what's left, clustering them and labelling with Qwen. \"As many objects as possible\" is in the brief, so more count should help, but only if the junk rate holds. Step 1 lets us check that.\n\n**4. Prove navigation with numbers (about 1 hour).**\n- Automatically check every route for clearance against the actual splats, reporting clipped routes out of 384.\n- Test the nearby display along a walk: does it show the right objects within range?\n- Render a sample of routes to check by eye, as an extra check.\n\n**5. A bigger copilot test (about 1 hour).** About 60 questions across several assets, including unknown ones, scored for \"correct\", not just \"passed the checks\". I'd also fix the blended confidence answer.\n\n**6. `make pipeline` and per-scene config (about 2–3 hours).** Backend is 15% and \"automated\" is in the criteria. It works without a second scan, by rerunning this room from scratch.\n\n## What I wouldn't do\n- **Chase the raw object count.** Splitting more or lowering thresholds would raise it, but the brief says number *and quality*, and judges will see junk boxes.\n- **Inflate the floor numbers.** Narrower bodies or looser filters would raise connected area while risking routes that clip.\n- **Quote 440 without the precision figure.** Together they're far more credible.\n\n## Priority against the rehearsal\nPR #13 and the 5090 rehearsal should still come first, since a demo that fails on the day costs more than any of these gain. But 1–5 only need Roihu, so I can run them alongside it.\n\nI'd start with step 1 now, as it tells us how much step 2 matters. Should I go ahead, and merge #13 too? And can someone spare 15 minutes to score the 60-object sample? A person's score is worth more on a slide than mine."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1971,"cache_read_input_tokens":699426,"output_tokens":2271,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":856},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1971,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2271,"cache_read_input_tokens":699426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1971},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dcc496a4-82cc-4866-bd5a-9b95e88d82ff","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoFEUEcstuez6sZ5EzP4","requestRef":"3f8f2a9b-8668-47ad-a894-277c1d781ab6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"83ae9d02-b87f-4aea-bb9d-70bffe632036","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:24:17.338Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/moving-splats","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
