{"parentUuid":"cb9b40de-0e08-453c-a4d6-085813bd9615","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoJdztaKqjdKoZzdRYNA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":754758,"output_tokens":1267,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":153},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":917,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":754758,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":917},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1101,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"d544ac41-049e-4370-8728-7c53bfe4ae5e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoJdeqqJwtBnTsZhZjcS","requestRef":"53daa4f5-ab60-4a04-a935-6d55009de72c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"138fb722-1806-460d-9d9c-074d05cf966a","timestamp":"2026-11-07T09:08:32.815Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/numbers","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"138fb722-1806-460d-9d9c-074d05cf966a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoJdztaKqjdKoZzdRYNA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Next is the 5090 rehearsal, then the submission items, which I haven't seen anything on yet.** The brief requires a working demo, a README, 5–8 slides, a video of up to 5 minutes and a technical note. Engineering is now ahead of those, so I'd move people onto them.\n\n## Order of work\n1. **Merge PR #14** to clear the failing check on `main`. It's waiting on your OK.\n2. **Rehearse on the 5090 and a tablet, offline.** Run this today, because it decides what can safely go in the video.\n3. **Record the demo video** as soon as the rehearsal works, so we have a safe copy, then re-record if things improve.\n4. **Write the slides, technical note and README** using the numbers we already have.\n5. **Improve the numbers** with whatever time is left, if CSC comes back.\n\n## Suggested split\n| Person | Own area | Now |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Viktor** | Coordination | Run the 5090 rehearsal, ask Valmet which pump is P-005, confirm the deadline, and chase CSC |\n| **Benjamin** | Viewer, tablet, video, slides | Test on a real tablet and choose which light scene it runs. Record the video and own the slides. Review the viewer changes made in his area |\n| **Eduard** | Backend, routing | Set up `make db` and `make api` on the 5090, and keep the router and offline networking working. Find a good second detour for the demo, and write the backend slide |\n| **Hannu** | Copilot, Excel | Score the 60-question copilot test by hand once it's run, and write the AI slide. Check the procedural mapping, and decide whether to keep `SKILL.md` |\n| **Sasha** | Extraction | Score the 60-object precision sample when CSC is back. Until then, write the extraction slide and technical note. If Sasha's own extraction branch is still separate, decide what to do with it |\n| **Me** | Whatever's unblocked | Write the 60 questions, draft the README, technical note and slide numbers from `docs/RESULTS.md`, fix what the rehearsal finds. When CSC returns, run the sample, label review, grouping and second pass |\n\nYou said earlier that you were working solo for now, so if the team isn't available, this is my order for you and me:\n- **You:** rehearsal, video, and Valmet's answer on P-005.\n- **Me:** everything written, plus fixes.\n\n## Who decides what\n- **Only a person can do:** the rehearsal, the tablet test, recording the video, asking Valmet, and scoring by hand if you want a human figure on the slides.\n- **What I can draft for review:** slides, technical note, README and its \"Pre-existing work\" section. Someone who knows what the team built before the hackathon should check that section.\n\n## Cut if time runs short\nIn this order:\n1. Voice mode\n2. Second-pass framing\n3. Pipe-run grouping\n4. Written directions\n\nI wouldn't cut the rehearsal, the video, the precision number or the copilot test.\n\n## Questions for you\n1. **Is the team back, or still solo?** That decides which split above applies.\n2. **Should I merge #14?**\n3. **Do you want me to start the written drafts now?** I'd recommend it. They don't depend on CSC or the 5090, and the README and technical note are required anyway. The slides could also be useful for the rehearsal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":754758,"output_tokens":1267,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":153},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":917,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1267,"cache_read_input_tokens":754758,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":917},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d544ac41-049e-4370-8728-7c53bfe4ae5e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoJdeqqJwtBnTsZhZjcS","requestRef":"53daa4f5-ab60-4a04-a935-6d55009de72c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"fe22f280-948e-47cd-b9e6-f55f44fc926f","timestamp":"2026-11-07T09:08:44.149Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/numbers","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
