{"parentUuid":"725de1de-0fd5-4685-bb6c-e8deec53ec92","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2dc4c464-d1a3-4398-9561-d703b137f8d6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ppGwUcKUrWBBSQwXa4Yf5","type":"tool_result","content":"viktor/numbers\n1:# Plan\n9:## The demo\n21:## Who does what\n32:## First tasks\n69:## Pipeline\n112:## Copilot\n119:### Example conversation\n136:### Tools\n146:### What the operator gets\n157:### How it should behave\n166:### Rules enforced in code\n174:### Keeping it reliable\n178:### Data limits\n182:## Where VLMs fit\n198:## Movable objects\n232:## Runs entirely on site\n241:### Compute estimates\n250:### Deployment at a plant (future)\n278:## Shared data\n292:## API\n304:## Milestones\n314:## Tracking results\n318:## Side challenges\n324:## Getting started\n# Since AI Hackathon 2026 — <team name>\n\n> A navigable digital twin of an industrial plant room for field service, running entirely on site.\n\nBuilt for Valmet's Industrial Metaverse challenge. It turns a Gaussian splat scan into framed,\nlabelled assets linked to device data, routes a worker around obstacles to a faulty device, and\ngives AI guidance with cited evidence. Runs on one local GPU server, viewed in a tablet browser.\n\n**Status:** in development. [Plan](docs/PLAN.md) · [Challenge](docs/CHALLENGE.md) ·\n[Results](docs/RESULTS.md)\n\n## Setup (once)\nNeeds: `git`, `make`, NVIDIA driver. One line (Linux) — installs uv, clones, sets up, checks GPU:\n```bash\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh && source ~/.local/bin/env && git clone https://github.com/Sai\n```\nShould end by printing your GPU name.\n\n## Commands\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `make db` | Start local TimescaleDB and load the Excel telemetry |\n| `make nav-check` | Test floor map, routes, mapping and API together, with a picture |\n| `make train` | Train a model |\n| `make tb` | Training graphs at http://localhost:6006 |\n| `make fmt` | Tidy code style and auto-fix lint |\n| `make check` | Lint and test: run before opening a PR |\n| `make entire` | Install and enable Entire |\n| `make views` | Download rendered views for the scene |\n| `make scene` | Download the demo scene, floor map, and objects |\n| `make pipeline` | Run a scene through everything, from `scenes/*.toml` |\n| `make model` | Download the copilot's language model (about 20 GB), before going offline |\n| `make scene-full` | Also download the full-quality scene (513 MB) |\n| `make up` | Train inside Docker |\n\n## Team workflow\n- Work on a `name/feature` branch, not `main`. Keep it small and merge within a couple of hours.\n- Rebase on `main`, run `make check`, then open a PR. CI must pass before merging.\n- Keep your handoff in `handoffs/<name>.md`, so a teammate or agent can pick up your work.\n- Coding agents follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).\n- Scenes and Valmet's data aren't in git. Get them from Viktor.\n- Run `make entire` once to set up session sharing and code search ([guide](docs/ENTIRE.md)).\n- Keys go in `.env` (copy `.env.example`), never in git.\n\n## Structure\n| Path | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `app/` | Pipeline, API, and copilot code ([who owns what](docs/PLAN.md)) |\n| `app/train.py` | Training template, not used by the demo so far |\n| `app/gpu_check.py` | GPU test |\n| `scripts/` | Frame selection, reconstruction, and Roihu jobs |\n| `fixtures/` | Fake sample data to build against |\n| `data/` | Datasets and generated scene files (not in git) |\n| `runs/` | Run outputs and saved models (not in git) |\n| `lumi/` | Run on the LUMI supercomputer ([guide](lumi/README.md)) |\n| `docs/` | Plan, challenge, results, pitch, Entire setup, live schedule |\n| `tests/` | Tests, run by `make test` and CI |\n| `handoffs/` | Each person's current status |\n\n## Pre-existing work\n\n## Who does what\nSwap freely if someone's skills fit another area better. Update this table and `AGENTS.md` if you do.\n\n| Person | Area | Folder | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Viktor** | Scene loading, cleaning, rendering, own splat | `app/scene/` | Enables all |\n| **Sasha** | Asset extraction, 3D boxes, splat tags | `app/extract/` | 30% |\n| **Eduard** | Floor, routing, nearby search, backend API | `app/nav/`, `app/api/` | 25% + 15% |\n| **Hannu** | Excel data, asset mapping, AI copilot | `app/copilot/` | 20% + part of 30% |\n| **Benjamin** | Web viewer, tablet, demo video, slides | `web/`, `docs/` | 10% + 25% display |\n\n## First tasks\n**Viktor**\n1. Write `app/scene/load.py`: read a splat PLY and filter it by opacity and size.\n2. Render color and depth views with known cameras, for Sasha to use.\n3. Check the COLMAP result, train 3DGS if it's clean, and compare it with `Equipment Room.ply`.\n4. Split the scene using `splat_labels.npy`: one PLY per object plus a background, each with a tint.\n\n**Sasha**\n1. Run SAM and CLIP on sample video frames to find which settings detect the most useful objects.\n\n## Scene input rule\nThe brief names Valmet's PLY as the input, but we have confirmation (reported by Viktor, 2026-11-06)\nthat we may use our own splat. Use it only if it beats `Equipment Room.ply`, and state which scene\nthe demo uses in the technical note.\n\n## Known data problems (as of 2026-11-06)\n- **`Industrial Boiler Room (1).ply` is damaged.** 67% of its records look like random bytes.\n  SHA-256 starts `117195366421b07a`. It's replaced by `Equipment Room.ply`.\ndocs/PLAN.md:26:| **Viktor** | Scene loading, cleaning, rendering, own splat | `app/scene/` | Enables all |\ndocs/PLAN.md:36:3. Check the COLMAP result, train 3DGS if it's clean, and compare it with `Equipment Room.ply`\ndocs/PLAN.md:72:Scene (.ply) → clean → render views → SAM → CLIP/VLM → 3D boxes ─→ assets.json\ndocs/PLAN.md:95:   background. Test this early, because it decides how clean moved objects look.\ndocs/PLAN.md:208:mixed up, and moved objects keep their old lighting. Pick the cleanest objects for the demo, \ndocs/PLAN.md:288:| `nav_grid.npz` | Eduard | Permanent occupancy grid, origin, cell size, and floor height |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9f2feb02-6c6a-41a6-a33b-2c06c00bb67d","timestamp":"2026-11-07T09:09:46.824Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"viktor/numbers\n1:# Plan\n9:## The demo\n21:## Who does what\n32:## First tasks\n69:## Pipeline\n112:## Copilot\n119:### Example conversation\n136:### Tools\n146:### What the operator gets\n157:### How it should behave\n166:### Rules enforced in code\n174:### Keeping it reliable\n178:### Data limits\n182:## Where VLMs fit\n198:## Movable objects\n232:## Runs entirely on site\n241:### Compute estimates\n250:### Deployment at a plant (future)\n278:## Shared data\n292:## API\n304:## Milestones\n314:## Tracking results\n318:## Side challenges\n324:## Getting started\n# Since AI Hackathon 2026 — <team name>\n\n> A navigable digital twin of an industrial plant room for field service, running entirely on site.\n\nBuilt for Valmet's Industrial Metaverse challenge. It turns a Gaussian splat scan into framed,\nlabelled assets linked to device data, routes a worker around obstacles to a faulty device, and\ngives AI guidance with cited evidence. Runs on one local GPU server, viewed in a tablet browser.\n\n**Status:** in development. [Plan](docs/PLAN.md) · [Challenge](docs/CHALLENGE.md) ·\n[Results](docs/RESULTS.md)\n\n## Setup (once)\nNeeds: `git`, `make`, NVIDIA driver. One line (Linux) — installs uv, clones, sets up, checks GPU:\n```bash\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh && source ~/.local/bin/env && git clone https://github.com/Sai\n```\nShould end by printing your GPU name.\n\n## Commands\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `make db` | Start local TimescaleDB and load the Excel telemetry |\n| `make nav-check` | Test floor map, routes, mapping and API together, with a picture |\n| `make train` | Train a model |\n| `make tb` | Training graphs at http://localhost:6006 |\n| `make fmt` | Tidy code style and auto-fix lint |\n| `make check` | Lint and test: