{"parentUuid":"7f07235e-eef7-450c-a86c-09d748576d3c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2dc4c464-d1a3-4398-9561-d703b137f8d6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019GAPZJEM4aVHTLNzdZQxLT","type":"tool_result","content":"AGENTS.md:10:  copy. Our own splat is allowed and replaces it only if it proves better. Keep scenes out of git.\nAGENTS.md:24:| Viktor | Scene loading, cleaning, rendering, own splat (`app/scene/`) |\nAGENTS.md:101:- A working demo beats clean abstractions. Avoid building for needs we don't have yet.\ndocs/CHALLENGE.md:65:that we may use our own splat. Use it only if it beats `Equipment Room.ply`, and state which scene\ndocs/PLAN.md:26:| **Viktor** | Scene loading, cleaning, rendering, own splat | `app/scene/` | Enables all |\ndocs/PLAN.md:36:3. Check the COLMAP result, train 3DGS if it's clean, and compare it with `Equipment Room.ply`.\ndocs/PLAN.md:72:Scene (.ply) → clean → render views → SAM → CLIP/VLM → 3D boxes ─→ assets.json\ndocs/PLAN.md:83:**Scene decided:** the demo uses the original `Equipment Room.ply`, because our own splat has holes in the floor. \ndocs/PLAN.md:88:1. **Clean (Viktor):** remove nearly transparent and oversized splats. Keep the original coordinates.\ndocs/PLAN.md:89:2. **Render (Viktor):** place cameras through the room and render color and depth. With our own splat,\ndocs/PLAN.md:95:   background. Test this early, because it decides how clean moved objects look.\ndocs/PLAN.md:247:| Building our own splat | CPU and 5090 | 1.5-3 hours more | About 8 GB RAM measured for COLMAP so far, up to 16 \n## Pipeline\n```text\nOFFLINE, once per scan\nScene (.ply) → clean → render views → SAM → CLIP/VLM → 3D boxes ─→ assets.json\n                 │                              └─ tag each splat ─→ splat_labels.npy\n                 │                                                       │\n                 │                               split scene ─→ objects/*.ply + background.ply\n                 │                                    Excel pack ─→ mapping.json\n## Getting started\n- **Scene and data:** get `Equipment Room.ply` and the Valmet folder from Viktor, not from git.\n- **Rendered views:** run `make views` (needs GitHub's `gh` CLI from cli.github.com, not the unrelated\n  `gh` package on PyPI, and `gh auth login`), or download the `views-v1` Release in\n  a browser and run `make views ARCHIVE=path/to/file.tar`. They go in `data/scene/equipment_room/`:\n  `render/` for the room, `render_detail/` for small objects. Each has `views/`, `depth/`, and\n  `cameras.json`. Delete Releases before making the repo public.\n- **Check your copy:** the SHA-256 of `Equipment Room.ply` starts `83d8c7d99316c08c`.\n- **GPU:** the 5090 is shared, so agree who's using it. Roihu needs `project_2020113` membership, so ask\n  Viktor. Most ThinkPads can only handle coding and the viewer.\n- **Git access:** the repo is private. Use SSH (`git remote set-url origin git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git`)\n  or log in with `gh auth login`.\n- **Merging:** merge small changes often, and tell the team when a shared file's format changes.\n# Pitch\n\nBrief asks for 5-8 slides and a demo video of 5 minutes at most. Benjamin owns these. Use only\nmeasured numbers from `docs/RESULTS.md`.\n\n1. **Problem:** a 3D scan looks real but knows nothing. Field-service staff and robots still have to\n   piece together location, equipment condition, and documentation from separate places.\n2. **Solution:** turn a scan into a navigable digital twin, on a tablet, running entirely on site.\n3. **Live demo:** tap an object, navigate to `P-005`, see nearby assets, get a cited diagnosis. Keep a\n   recorded backup ready.\n4. **3D semantic extraction:** how a splat becomes framed, labelled assets, and how many.\n5. **Pathfinding:** floor, obstacles, and a route that doesn't pass through anything.\n6. **Metadata mapping:** how Excel records attach to objects, with confidence and no invented IDs.\n7. **AI approach:** local copilot with citations, confidence, and safe next steps, not autonomous\n   action.\n8. **Impact and next steps:** no plant data leaves the site. Say what a real rollout would still need,\n   such as live data and real-world positioning.\n78:## Commands\n79-| Command | Use |\n80-|---|---|","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fd8c6dcb-c511-4ecf-af7c-5293760ea673","timestamp":"2026-11-07T09:09:55.710Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"AGENTS.md:10:  copy. Our own splat is allowed and replaces it only if it proves better. Keep scenes out of git.\nAGENTS.md:24:| Viktor | Scene loading, cleaning, rendering, own splat (`app/scene/`) |\nAGENTS.md:101:- A working demo beats clean abstractions. Avoid building for needs we don't have yet.\ndocs/CHALLENGE.md:65:that we may use our own splat. Use it only if it beats `Equipment Room.ply`, and state which scene\ndocs/PLAN.md:26:| **Viktor** | Scene loading, cleaning, rendering, own splat | `app/scene/` | Enables all |\ndocs/PLAN.md:36:3. Check the COLMAP result, train 3DGS if it's clean, and compare it with `Equipment Room.ply`.\ndocs/PLAN.md:72:Scene (.ply) → clean → render views → SAM → CLIP/VLM → 3D boxes ─→ assets.json\ndocs/PLAN.md:83:**Scene decided:** the demo uses the original `Equipment Room.ply`, because our own splat has holes in the floor. \ndocs/PLAN.md:88:1. **Clean (Viktor):** remove nearly transparent and oversized splats. Keep the original coordinates.\ndocs/PLAN.md:89:2. **Render (Viktor):** place cameras through the room and render color and depth. With our own splat,\ndocs/PLAN.md:95:   background. Test this early, because it decides how clean moved objects look.\ndocs/PLAN.md:247:| Building our own splat | CPU and 5090 | 1.5-3 hours more | About 8 GB RAM measured for COLMAP so far, up to 16 \n## Pipeline\n```text\nOFFLINE, once per scan\nScene (.ply) → clean → render views → SAM → CLIP/VLM → 3D boxes ─→ assets.json\n                 │                              └─ tag each splat ─→ splat_labels.npy\n                 │                                                       │\n                 │                               split scene ─→ objects/*.ply + background.ply\n                 │                                    Excel pack ─→ mapping.json\n## Getting started\n- **Scene and data:** get `Equipment Room.ply` and the Valmet folder from Viktor, not from git.\n- **Rendered views:** run `make views` (needs GitHub's `gh` CLI from cli.github.com, not the unrelated\n  `gh` package on PyPI, and `gh auth login`), or download the `views-v1` Release in\n  a browser and run `make views ARCHIVE=path/to/file.tar`. They go in `data/scene/equipment_room/`:\n  `render/` for the room, `render_detail/` for small objects. Each has `views/`, `depth/`, and\n  `cameras.json`. Delete Releases before making the repo public.\n- **Check your copy:** the SHA-256 of `Equipment Room.ply` starts `83d8c7d99316c08c`.\n- **GPU:** the 5090 is shared, so agree who's using it. Roihu needs `project_2020113` membership, so ask\n  Viktor. Most ThinkPads can only handle coding and the viewer.\n- **Git access:** the repo is private. Use SSH (`git remote set-url origin git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git`)\n  or log in with `gh auth login`.\n- **Merging:** merge small changes often, and tell the team when a shared file's format changes.\n# Pitch\n\nBrief asks for 5-8 slides and a demo video of 5 minutes at most. Benjamin owns these. Use only\nmeasured numbers from `docs/RESULTS.md`.\n\n1. **Problem:** a 3D scan looks real but knows nothing. Field-service staff and robots still have to\n   piece together location, equipment condition, and documentation from separate places.\n2. **Solution:** turn a scan into a navigable digital twin, on a tablet, running entirely on site.\n3. **Live demo:** tap an object, navigate to `P-005`, see nearby assets, get a cited diagnosis. Keep a\n   recorded backup ready.\n4. **3D semantic extraction:** how a splat becomes framed, labelled assets, and how many.\n5. **Pathfinding:** floor, obstacles, and a route that doesn't pass through anything.\n6. **Metadata mapping:** how Excel records attach to objects, with confidence and no invented IDs.\n7. **AI approach:** local copilot with citations, confidence, and safe next steps, not autonomous\n   action.\n8. **Impact and next steps:** no plant data leaves the site. Say what a real rollout would still need,\n   such as live data and real-world positioning.\n78:## Commands\n79-| Command | Use |\n80-|---|---|","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e38d568a-fa7a-48fe-9fe7-78be4ff5f1fa","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","branch":"viktor/numbers","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":null,"remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7f07235e-eef7-450c-a86c-09d748576d3c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/numbers","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
