{"parentUuid":"f06bb5b5-f8d3-49d9-9a38-9996beac55ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoJkHhna8YR9CNkvMgLL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019twx6w53rKUJpuVrf4URq3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='docs/PLAN.md'; t=open(p).read()\na=t.index('## First tasks'); b=t.index('## Pipeline')\nt=t[:a]+'''## Now\nThe core works, so the priority is proving it on real hardware and finishing the submission. Submit\nSunday 09:00, deadline 10:00, per an earlier doc: Viktor is confirming this. Current state is in\n`handoffs/` and measured numbers are in `docs/RESULTS.md`.\n\n**In order:** 5090 and tablet rehearsal offline, record a safe demo video, slides, technical note, and\nREADME, then improve numbers if time remains.\n\n| Person | Task now |\n|---|---|\n| **Viktor** | Run the 5090 rehearsal. Ask Valmet which pump is `P-005`. Confirm the deadline. Find out why CSC SSH is unreachable |\n| **Benjamin** | Test on a real tablet and pick its light scene. Record the video. Own the slides. Review the viewer changes |\n| **Eduard** | Set up `make db` and `make api` on the 5090, plus the router and offline network. Find a second good detour. Backend slide |\n| **Hannu** | Score the 60-question copilot test by hand. AI slide. Check the procedural links. Decide whether `skills/` belongs in this repo |\n| **Sasha** | Score the 60-object precision sample once CSC is back. Extraction slide and technical note. Retire or merge the old extraction branch |\n| **Coding agents** | Draft the README and notes from measured numbers, fix what the rehearsal finds, then run the sample, label review, grouping, and second pass when CSC returns |\n\n**Cut first if short of time:** voice mode, second-pass framing, pipe runs, written directions. Don't cut\nthe rehearsal, video, precision number, or copilot test.\n\n**Say this accurately:** four objects move as real splats, and the others as outlines. `P-005` on\n`obj-0049` is an unconfirmed pick. 29 of 30 Excel links are procedural. `P-005`'s record only has\npressure and flow data. The floor under moved objects is copied, not scanned. Position is simulated.\n\n### Run the demo on the 5090\nPut `Equipment Room.ply` in `data/scene/equipment_room/` and the Excel pack in `data/`, then, with\ninternet: `make scene mapping db model pieces`. Offline, in two terminals:\n```text\nmake api\nmake web SCENE=data/scene/equipment_room/cut/base.ply ASSETS=data/scene/equipment_room/assets_mapped.json SHAPES=data/scene/equipment_room/shapes.json PIECES=data/scene/equipment_room/cut\n```\nDemo move: plan to `P-005` from the room centre, then drag the roll cage `obj-0067` onto the route near\n(-1.46, -1.75). The route goes from 4.3 to 5.6 m. **Undo changes** restores it.\n\n'''+t[b:]\nt=t.replace(\"| **Viktor** | Scene loading, cleaning, rendering, own splat | `app/scene/` | Enables all |\",\"| **Viktor** | Scene loading, rendering, moving objects, floor patch | `app/scene/` | Enables all |\")\nt=t.replace(\"Scene (.ply) → clean → render views → SAM\",\"Scene (.ply) → render views → SAM\")\nt=re.sub(r\"\\*\\*Scene decided:\\*\\* the demo uses the original `Equipment Room.ply`, because our own splat has holes in the floor\\.\",\"**Scene decided:** the demo uses the original, uncleaned `Equipment Room.ply`. It's more complete and looks far better away from any filmed path.\",t)\nt=t.replace(\"1. **Clean (Viktor):** remove nearly transparent and oversized splats. Keep the original coordinates.\",\"1. **No cleaning for anything people see:** `clean_mask` left black holes (22.32 to 16.59 dB in a test). It's for analysis such as floor maps only.\")\nt=t.replace(\"- **Rendered views:** run `make views` (needs GitHub's `gh` CLI from cli.github.com, not the unrelated\\n  `gh` package on PyPI, and `gh auth login`), or download the `views-v1` Release in\\n  a browser and run `make views ARCHIVE=path/to/file.tar`. They go in `data/scene/equipment_room/`:\\n  `render/` for the room, `render_detail/` for small objects. Each has `views/`, `depth/`, and\\n  `cameras.json`. Delete Releases before making the repo public.\\n\",\"- **Objects, floor map, light scenes:** run `make scene` (needs GitHub's `gh` CLI from cli.github.com,\\n  not the unrelated `gh` package on PyPI, and `gh auth login`). It gets Release `objects-v2`. Object IDs\\n  changed from `objects-v1`, so rerun `make mapping`. Skip `make views`, `make scene-full`, and `make floor`:\\n  they use old renders, our own splat, or rebuild a worse map without the render folders.\\n  Delete all Releases before making the repo public.\\n\")\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n\np='AGENTS.md'; t=open(p).read()\nt=t.replace('''- Scene input is Valmet's restored `Equipment Room.ply`, not the damaged `Industrial Boiler Room`\n  copy. Our own splat is allowed and replaces it only if it proves better. Keep scenes out of git.\n''','''- The demo scene is Valmet's uncleaned `Equipment Room.ply`. Don't use the damaged `Industrial Boiler\n  Room` copy or our own splat, which looks worse. Keep scenes out of git. Never run `clean_mask` on\n  anything people see or that views are rendered from: it leaves black holes.\n- Current tasks and how to run the demo: `docs/PLAN.md`, under \"Now\".\n''')\nt=t.replace(\"| Viktor | Scene loading, cleaning, rendering, own splat (`app/scene/`) |\",\"| Viktor | Scene loading, rendering, moving objects (`app/scene/`) |\")\nt=t.replace('''| `make train` | Train a model |\n''','''| `make scene` | Get objects, floor map, and light scenes: then `make mapping` |\n| `make pieces` | Cut movable objects out of the scene |\n| `make model` | Get the copilot's language model, before going offline |\n| `make pipeline` | Run a scene through everything, from `scenes/*.toml` |\n| `make train` | Train a model |\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n\np='README.md'; t=open(p).read()\nt=t.replace('''**Status:** in development. [Plan](docs/PLAN.md)''','''**Status:** core features work, not yet rehearsed on the demo hardware.\n[Current tasks and how to run the demo](docs/PLAN.md#now) · [Plan](docs/PLAN.md)''')\nt=t.replace('''| `make views` | Download rendered views for the scene |\n| `make scene` | Download the demo scene, floor map, and objects |\n''','''| `make scene` | Download objects, floor map, and light scenes |\n| `make mapping` | Link Excel records to objects, marking how each was linked |\n| `make pieces` | Cut movable objects out of the scene, so dragging moves the real thing |\n''')\nt=t.replace(\"| `make scene-full` | Also download the full-quality scene (513 MB) |\\n\",\"\")\nt=t.replace(\"| `scripts/` | Frame selection, reconstruction, and Roihu jobs |\\n\",\"| `scripts/` | Pipeline, route check, copilot test, frame selection, and Roihu jobs |\\n| `scenes/` | One settings file per scene, for `make pipeline` |\\n\")\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n\np='docs/CHALLENGE.md'; t=open(p).read()\nt=t.replace('''that we may use our own splat. Use it only if it beats `Equipment Room.ply`, and state which scene\nthe demo uses in the technical note.\n''','''that we may use our own splat. We compared them and the demo uses the uncleaned `Equipment Room.ply`,\nso say that in the technical note.\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n\np='docs/PITCH.md'; t=open(p).read()\nt=t.replace('''4. **3D semantic extraction:** how a splat becomes framed, labelled assets, and how many.\n5. **Pathfinding:** floor, obstacles, and a route that doesn't pass through anything.\n''','''4. **3D semantic extraction:** how a splat becomes framed, labelled assets, and how many. Show the count\n   with the precision sample, not the count alone.\n5. **Pathfinding:** floor, obstacles, and a route that doesn't pass through anything. Show the route check\n   and the live detour when the roll cage moves.\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n\np='handoffs/viktortrilar.md'\nopen(p,'w').write(\"\"\"# viktortrilar: main (viktor/numbers merged)\n**Goal:** demo on Valmet's uncleaned scene, then measure and improve the scored numbers\n**Done:** route check, `make pipeline`, per-scene config, configurable copilot default. Docs updated: tasks and demo steps are in docs/PLAN.md under \"Now\"\n**Verified:** lint; 189 tests passed, 2 skipped. 383 of 384 routes touch fewer than 10 splats. `make pipeline` has only had a dry run. Not tested: 5090, tablet, model text in the browser panel\n**Next:** rehearse on the 5090. Ask Valmet which pump is P-005. When CSC returns: 60-object precision sample, label review, grouping check, second pass, real pipeline run. Write the 60-question copilot test\n**Blockers:** SSH to Roihu, Puhti and Mahti times out from two networks, no maintenance announced. Use `ssh -4` on networks without IPv6. Cert valid to 2026-11-07 20:41. Local branch viktor/viewer-objects holds an unused merge: don't merge it\n\"\"\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | tail -8 | cut -c1-60; awk 'length>0' AGENTS.md | wc -l; make lint 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; git add AGENTS.md README.md docs handoffs/viktortrilar.md; git commit -qm \"Update the docs for the current demo, tasks, and team split\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"; git fetch -q origin; git merge origin/main --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-50; git push -q git@github.com:Sairanyx/Newbies.git viktor/numbers 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-30; sleep 25; gh pr checks 14 --watch --interval 8 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-40; gh pr view 14 --json mergeable --jq .mergeable; gh pr merge 14 --merge 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-90; sleep 4; gh pr view 14 --json state --jq .state; git fetch -q origin; git log --oneline -1 origin/main | cut -c1-80; sleep 20; gh run list --branch main --limit 1 --json conclusion,status,headSha --jq '.[]|\"main \\(.headSha[:7]) \\(.status) \\(.conclusion)\"'","description":"Update the docs, push, wait for CI, and merge PR 14","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_seque