{"parentUuid":"0e6d9f8e-f92a-4196-90b2-8828150b809b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoKZngsb2JWCbAwDBzuA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1496,"cache_read_input_tokens":781950,"output_tokens":1186,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":36},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1496,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1186,"cache_read_input_tokens":781950,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1496},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6608,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"3a3cf9db-ff3f-4ff4-b4f0-e6aecce25403","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoKZnDbEi1fTx9S62DpM","requestRef":"ac367b85-173c-45e1-a0ac-138e7ce2e536","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"05110124-f076-4a2f-a174-868f9d7cc11f","timestamp":"2026-11-07T09:20:47.674Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/move-sync","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"05110124-f076-4a2f-a174-868f9d7cc11f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoKZngsb2JWCbAwDBzuA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed real bugs that could explain what Sasha is seeing, and the usage guide is written, but I don't know yet which problem Sasha hit. It's all in [PR #16](https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/16), not merged, and CI was still running when I last checked. All 189 tests pass locally (2 skipped). The guide is `docs/USAGE.md`, linked from the README.\n\n## What happens when you move an object\n1. **Tap the object.** The viewer selects the smallest box under your finger and opens the panel.\n2. **Press Move on floor.** Only objects marked movable get this button.\n3. **Drag.** The box, fitted shape and scan piece all move, but only on your screen so far.\n4. **Release.** The viewer sends the new position to `POST /api/changes`, through `web/serve.py` to the backend on port 8001.\n5. **The backend saves it.** It refuses anything not movable, updates the object's box and logs the change. It's kept in memory, plus the database if `make db` is running.\n6. **The route re-plans,** if one is showing. The floor map itself never changes: movable objects are added on top as blockers for each route, which is why the route bends.\n7. **Reloading** now fetches `/api/assets` and restores saved moves.\n8. **Undo changes** calls `/api/changes/reset`.\n\n## What was probably breaking for Sasha\n| Problem | Before | Now |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Reloading the page** | Objects jumped back on screen, while routes still avoided their new spots | Moves are restored |\n| **Releasing the mouse outside the canvas** | Stuck in move mode | The drag finishes |\n| **Backend not running** | No warning until you moved something | Warned on load |\n| **`make web` and `make api` using different files** | Moves failed with a confusing error | Warned on load |\n| **Object can't move** | The button just wasn't there | The panel says why |\n\n**Not a bug, but it looks like one:** only four objects move as the real scan: `obj-0067`, `obj-0021`, `obj-0008` and `obj-0112`. The other movable objects only move as an outline, so they look like they aren't moving in Scan view. The four also need `make pieces` and `PIECES=` on the `make web` line. Sasha should test with the roll cage, `obj-0067`.\n\n## For Sasha to try\n```bash\ngit fetch && git switch viktor/move-sync\nmake scene mapping pieces\nmake api      # first terminal\nmake web SCENE=data/scene/equipment_room/cut/base.ply ASSETS=data/scene/equipment_room/assets_mapped.json SHAPES=data/scene/equipment_room/shapes.json PIECES=data/scene/equipment_room/cut      # second terminal\n```\nThen press **Go to P-005**, tap the roll cage, press **Move on floor**, and drag it onto the route.\n\nIf it still fails, I need three things from Sasha: the message in the top-left panel, any red errors in the browser console (F12), and which object they tried.\n\n**Tested:** no backend, mismatched files, a real mouse drag, releasing over a button, reload, fixed objects and undo, in a browser on a light scene with software rendering. **Not tested:** a tablet, and the 5090.\n\nShould I merge #16 once CI passes? Sasha can use the branch in the meantime. Number 15 also seems to exist, and I haven't looked at it, so someone else may have a PR open too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1496,"cache_read_input_tokens":781950,"output_tokens":1186,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":36},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1496,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1186,"cache_read_input_tokens":781950,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1496},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3a3cf9db-ff3f-4ff4-b4f0-e6aecce25403","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoKZnDbEi1fTx9S62DpM","requestRef":"ac367b85-173c-45e1-a0ac-138e7ce2e536","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"80638ece-fdd5-4b80-a47f-c19cd937c019","timestamp":"2026-11-07T09:20:51.629Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/move-sync","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
