{"parentUuid":"75f2c44a-daa0-4c81-b182-1bfe566a0e2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoP626wnu5JSqLNf2Sje","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_read_input_tokens":815936,"output_tokens":1319,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":47},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":815936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6993,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"fd4ee033-a13c-4ee9-99f4-ef75eb0760a3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoP61XEHYvAzNFdQscaQ","requestRef":"3db6db6e-01c4-42fe-8550-d50f88556e95","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"bfe6a382-0876-49ac-a409-599fb22d9afa","timestamp":"2026-11-07T10:06:58.730Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/move-collisions","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"bfe6a382-0876-49ac-a409-599fb22d9afa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoP626wnu5JSqLNf2Sje","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Collisions are done and in [PR #18](https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/18), with CI passing but not merged. CSC is still down, and I think a small BIM export is worth doing, after the rehearsal.**\n\n## Collisions\nWhen you drag an object somewhere it doesn't fit, the object and whatever's blocking it turn see-through red, drawn over everything. The panel turns red too and says why, such as \"It would overlap cart obj-0047\". Releasing there puts it back at its last good spot.\n\nThe backend enforces this as well, so nothing can save a bad position. A direct API call gets refused with a 409. All 198 tests pass (2 skipped), and in the browser the demo move still gives the 4.31 to 5.56 m detour, with undo working.\n\n| A move is refused if | A move is still allowed if |\n|---|---|\n| It overlaps another object's box by 15% or more | It's a slight touch, since boxes are loose |\n| Less than 80% of its footprint is free floor, or its centre isn't | The object passes under something overhead |\n| | The object it touches is a cable, hose or tiny fragment |\n| | The object was carried inside its own box at the start |\n\n**One thing you might notice:** a move is only refused if it's worse than where the object started. The room is so cluttered that only 12 of 59 movable objects counted as clear where they stand under the plain rule, so without this most couldn't move at all.\n\n**Limits:**\n- Boxes are approximate, so it will sometimes refuse a real gap or allow a small real overlap. On open floor, 270–362 of 400 random spots are allowed, depending on the object.\n- Newly added objects get an overlap warning, not a refusal.\n- It hasn't been tested on a tablet or the 5090.\n\n## CSC\nRoihu still times out, and Puhti and Mahti gave no answer at last check. It's been over an hour, so I'd email servicedesk@csc.fi if nobody on the team can log in. The demo doesn't need CSC, but the precision sample and label review do.\n\n## What is 3D to BIM?\nI haven't seen the engineer's resources, so this is the general idea. **BIM (Building Information Modelling)** is the structured model of a building that engineers work in: every element is a typed object, like a pump, pipe or wall, with properties and relationships. \"Scan-to-BIM\" means turning a scan into that model. The usual open format is IFC, supported by tools like Revit and Bonsai.\n\nIt's close to what we already do: a scan becomes typed objects with data attached.\n\n**Would it make the project better?** Partly:\n- **Worth doing, a small IFC export:** each object becomes an IFC element with its box, type, Excel link, and how it was linked and how confident we are. It should be about half a day, using the open-source IfcOpenShell library, which I haven't tried here. It would make our output usable in engineers' own tools, which fits extraction and backend, and could impress an engineer who shared these resources.\n- **Not worth it now, real BIM geometry:** BIM models use accurate parametric pipes and walls. Our boxes are rough, 158 objects have unknown mobility, and scale isn't verified, so we shouldn't claim real BIM. It's fair to say \"BIM-ready export of detected objects, for review\".\n- **Not in the brief.** It wouldn't directly score, unless the engineer's interest counts as a signal, as it did with moving objects.\n\n## Next\n1. **Merge #18?** Sasha's testing would benefit.\n2. **Can you send me the engineer's resources?** Or ask what they'd most like to see, since that decides whether BIM is a nice extra or a real priority. Moving objects was extra credit because the engineer said so.\n3. **Rehearse on the 5090.** It's still the biggest risk, and I'd do it before starting BIM. Has it happened yet?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_read_input_tokens":815936,"output_tokens":1319,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":47},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":815936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fd4ee033-a13c-4ee9-99f4-ef75eb0760a3","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoP61XEHYvAzNFdQscaQ","requestRef":"3db6db6e-01c4-42fe-8550-d50f88556e95","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"31574f4e-0476-4cb9-bf22-5305fd46b1cc","timestamp":"2026-11-07T10:07:05.071Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/move-collisions","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
