{"parentUuid":"7cc2cf0e-e20e-488b-a683-e9959143e28d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoQTqcPifyUepyNQL1we","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1598,"cache_read_input_tokens":855778,"output_tokens":1421,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1598,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1421,"cache_read_input_tokens":855778,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1598},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8809,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"87573249-6365-41f0-8d7f-e56b0e82c7ac","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoQTq88TdEaB8fiqKt1G","requestRef":"5b1411e7-a4ca-43cc-aa42-d18a48faa7f6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"3e7c7213-1848-47fd-9a54-173fb57762af","timestamp":"2026-11-07T10:25:03.415Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/split-and-occlusion","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"3e7c7213-1848-47fd-9a54-173fb57762af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoQTqcPifyUepyNQL1we","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Split, Combine and the cleaner frames are done, but neither they nor the collision check are on `main` yet.** They're in [PR #22](https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/22), stacked on [PR #18](https://github.com/Sairanyx/Newbies/pull/18), and CI passes on #22. All 205 tests passed, though that ran before the teammates' merges below.\n\n## What's new\n- **Split:** tap an object and press **Split into two**, then drag a box around one part. Orange is your selection and blue is the rest. The model suggests labels, code sets mobility by rule when it does, and you confirm.\n- **Combine:** tap an object, press **Combine with...**, then tap the second. An orange box goes around both for you to confirm. I tested this with a real tap.\n- **Frames:** a nearer box now hides what's behind it, so the tank's lines stop at the chair's box, and each box's own back edges are gone. The scan shows no holes.\n- **Safety and undo:** split and combined objects survive a reload, and **Undo changes** restores the originals. Objects linked to a record, like P-005, are refused so that a link can't be lost or guessed.\n\n**Limits:**\n- Parts of a split or combined object move as outlines, because the scan piece doesn't split with them.\n- The roll cage and chair `obj-0021` are affected if split, and they'd need `make pieces` rerun with new cuts.\n- From a cluttered view, your selection can land on a small object in front. In my test, a tap meant for a pipe selected `obj-0366`. The panel names both objects before you save.\n\n**Two corrections:**\n- Your screenshot showed `obj-0008`'s star base was gone, so I took it off the moving list. Three objects now move as real splats: `obj-0067`, `obj-0021` and `obj-0112`.\n- Rerun `make pieces` after pulling, or the old cut stays in use.\n\n## What Roihu's closure means\nIt's closed until at least Monday, which is likely after the deadline. **The demo isn't affected,** because everything it needs is in Release `objects-v2`. Any job already running would continue, but none of mine are.\n\n| No longer possible from Roihu | What we can do instead |\n|---|---|\n| Precision sample and label review (needed its masks) | Render crops from each object's box on the 5090, and score those. It looks a bit different, but it's still a real number |\n| Second-pass framing, re-running extraction | Needs SAM set up on the 5090. I wouldn't start that now |\n| Real `make pipeline` run | Say it's built but not fully run, unless the 5090 gets SAM |\n| 60-question copilot test | Not affected: it can run on the 5090 |\n\nIts masks, full renders and video frames had no other copy, so they're out of reach until it reopens. **The 5090 is now our only GPU,** so the team needs to agree who's using it.\n\n## Before merging\nTeammates merged into `main` while I worked: Sasha's cyan highlight on selected objects (#19), and Benjamin's merge (#21), which brought in Eduard's live re-planning and route arrows. Git reports no conflicts with my branches, but **these features have never run together**, and they touch the same code:\n- Sasha's highlight hides the selected box, which could hide my red warning.\n- Eduard's live re-planning and my re-plan after a move both act on routes.\n\nSo I'd merge #18 and #22, then run the full browser test on the merged result right away, fixing anything it finds.\n\n**Should I merge #18 and #22 now?** I'd also tell the team to pause viewer merges for a few minutes while I do that test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1598,"cache_read_input_tokens":855778,"output_tokens":1421,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1598,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1421,"cache_read_input_tokens":855778,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1598},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"87573249-6365-41f0-8d7f-e56b0e82c7ac","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoQTq88TdEaB8fiqKt1G","requestRef":"5b1411e7-a4ca-43cc-aa42-d18a48faa7f6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"224abb96-7dbe-43b5-84e2-9387dffd3ec5","timestamp":"2026-11-07T10:25:09.471Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/split-and-occlusion","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
