{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","id":"848f62f2-1a28-4ee4-ba0e-e226282f5b64","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:27:41.779Z","version":"2.1.319","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"80685e5874ec7369d5453564df649646f599e1d2b04108a0965cd86f4c7bfa44","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"858e9e03-bde5-4015-a01a-de3b00e02cc4","keep":626,"tail":["8f51e14aedfc4942ab3bb241f32ab8b1cd5f4a454f7b3d4b9602a0b836555d50","d66d575ed03975a41c6a0761d077b71da25b0ad0dd2fec0d01b934fdf4ea76eb"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",627,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8059378c66e78928b10866950ce9d961cf6b49bbab559c765073e73276251a50"}
{"parentUuid":"76c25768-c40e-4176-99b2-4965eb90b630","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoVFhax8ivRkr9Gh4cAL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**All merged: `main` (`92d3cd5`) has everything, passes CI, and no PRs are open.** All 213 tests pass locally (2 skipped).\n\n## What I reviewed and merged\n| PR | From | What it adds |\n|---|---|---|\n| #18 | Viktor | Collision check, red warning |\n| #19 | Sasha, already merged | Cyan highlight on selected objects |\n| #20 | Eduard | Handoff update only |\n| #21 | Benjamin, already merged | Route arrows, and Eduard's live route updates |\n| #22 | Viktor | Split, Combine, frames that hide what's behind them |\n| #23 | Hannu | Removes the `skills` file and ignores that folder |\n\nI opened #23 for Hannu because his branch had no PR. It only does what his commit says.\n\n## Problems the review found\nThe features worked on their own, but clashed once combined. All of these are fixed:\n- **Route vanishing:** live routes followed the camera even in fly mode, so just looking around could wipe the route. They now follow you only in walk mode. **Eduard should know**, since this changes his feature.\n- **Bent route after a refused drop:** the route stayed bent around a spot the object never reached. It now re-plans.\n- **Hidden warnings:** route messages overwrote \"Can't place it here\", and the split and combine success messages.\n- **Missing highlight:** new parts from Split or Combine now get Sasha's highlight when selected, though parts without a segmented surface just show a message.\n\n## Tested together\nIn one browser run, with pieces, highlights and live routes all on, and no page errors:\n- Refused drop: goes red, then returns with the route restored\n- Demo move: 4.31 to 5.56 m\n- Split, then combine\n- Reload keeps every change, and undo restores everything\n\nThis used software rendering on a light scene with the template copilot. The second-object step of Combine was called directly here, though a real tap passed in the earlier test. While dragging, the preview route can lag on slow machines: it showed 3.81 m just before the object settled to 5.56 m, and that's worth watching on the 5090.\n\n## For the team\n```bash\ngit pull\nmake scene mapping pieces highlights\n```\n- **`make pieces` needs rerunning,** because `obj-0008` came off the moving list.\n- **`make highlights` is new,** and `make web` picks it up automatically.\n- `docs/USAGE.md` covers Split, Combine and the rest.\n\n## Next\n1. **Rehearse on the 5090.** This is now the priority by a long way: nothing has run on real hardware, and we've added a lot today.\n2. **Ask Valmet's engineer** which pump is P-005, and what they'd want from BIM. Can you send me those resources?\n3. **Start the required submission items:** video, slides, technical note, README. I can draft the written ones now, if you want. Roihu's closure means the precision sample has to come from crops rendered on the 5090, and I can write that script too.\n\nWhich should I start on?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1093,"cache_read_input_tokens":884149,"output_tokens":988,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1093,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":988,"cache_read_input_tokens":884149,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1093},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"af05acdf-3328-4c72-88c1-5e5b556a75cc","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoVFgxzLzJhd5FfVELNn","requestRe