| cut -c1-125; sed -n 7,20p docs/USAGE.md | cut -c1-90; grep -n \"Walk\\b\\|mode\" web/index.html | head -3 | cut -c1-70","description":"Check the usage guide against what's now on main","timeout":15000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"73b821f5-e332-46ac-937b-1f1bfe63f9e8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoVKQEGukdNeH2GhG2iq","requestRef":"12a03e4f-6daf-4f82-ac2d-2dcc536404e8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b0366835-c3fd-43e4-92e4-7d61ce44b26d","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:28:37.145Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"main","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"b0366835-c3fd-43e4-92e4-7d61ce44b26d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2feca5d4-6303-4839-8b4a-8174acce4ee6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HLEaRezXaowRLDGSbPCh49","type":"tool_result","content":"main\n5:## Set up\n21:## Run it\n32:## Highlight an object's surface\n47:## Move an object\n63:### What happens when you move something\n82:## Add a missed object\n88:## Split an object that's really two things\n95:## Combine objects that are really one thing\n100:## Ask the copilot\n104:## Other controls\n118:## If something's wrong\n14:make pieces     # cuts movable objects out of the scene\n15:make highlights # exports cyan segmented surfaces for object selection\n30:`make pieces PIECES_FROM=data/scene/equipment_room/light_full.ply`\n32:## Highlight an object's surface\n33:Run `make highlights`, then restart your viewer. Clicking an object tints its segmented\n34:splats cyan and hides its selected box; selecting another object replaces the highlight.\n35:The highlight follows dragging and undo and is independent of the **Boxes** toggle.\n37:The four cut-out movable objects highlight their whole cut piece, the same splats that move when\n38:dragged, so run `make pieces` before `make highlights`. Other objects show detected surfaces only:\n42:Generate highlights from the original PLY, not `cut/base.ply` or a reduced scene: labels index the\n43:original scene. Generated highlights are loaded automatically for scenes under `SCENE_DIR`.\n44:For a different scene, pass its own `HIGHLIGHTS=path/to/highlights`, or disable loading with\n45:`HIGHLIGHTS=`.\n50:3. Drag anywhere on the screen. The object follows your drag across the floor.\n52:   - If the spot is taken, the object and whatever's in its way turn red, and the panel says why.\n53:   - Releasing on a red spot puts it back at the last good spot. A wall or fixed equipment blocks it too.\n59:Three objects move as the real scan: `obj-0067`, `obj-0021`, and `obj-0112`. Other movable objects\n68:                      POST /api/objects/ID/check-move: app/api/collisions.py says if it fits, for the red warning\n74:Route showing?        web/route.js: POST /api/route from the route's same start\n84:2. Check the orange box. Use **Bigger** or **Smaller** if it's off.\n88:## Split an object that's really two things\n89:1. Tap the object, and press **Split into two**. Objects linked to a record can't be split.\n90:2. Drag a box around one part. Orange is what you selected, and blue is the rest.\n95:## Combine objects that are really one thing\n96:1. Tap the first object, and press **Combine with...**. Objects linked to a record can't be combined.\n97:2. Tap the second object. An orange box appears around both.\n110:| **Range** | How far away frames and labels show |\n125:| Box goes red and panel says \"Can't place it here\" | That spot is taken | Drop it somewhere else. Tiny overlaps are allo\n126:| Only an outline moves | Not one of the three objects, or no `PIECES=` | Use the full `make web` line above |\n136:Open the browser's developer console (F12) for more detail, and include any red errors when asking for help.\n- `Equipment Room.ply`, in `data/scene/equipment_room/`\n- The Excel pack, in `data/`, as any `.xlsx` file\n\n```bash\ngit pull\nmake scene      # objects, floor map, and light scenes\nmake mapping    # links Excel records to objects, writes assets_mapped.json\nmake pieces     # cuts movable objects out of the scene\nmake highlights # exports cyan segmented surfaces for object selection\nmake db         # optional, needs Docker: keeps changes after a restart\nmake model      # optional, about 20 GB: the copilot's language model\n```\nRun these with internet. The demo itself needs none.\n\n36:    <button id=\"follow\" hidden>Walk route</button>\n40:    <button id=\"mode\">Walk</button>\n44:    <button id=\"view-mode\">Scan</button>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8a29e8cd-29f5-4717-8d99-ec5de0911cd1","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:28