cription":"Read the shared repo's description and README","timeout":20000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd4f81bc-6c96-47c5-a1de-ef479aed4db4","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgoVQwRe6ksftJiYpxoKy","requestRef":"0c74ad7b-1210-4b38-895e-752a86bb65a2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c5c4aec-6951-405a-85c2-03819d5b1512","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:29:55.397Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/usage-update","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"4c5c4aec-6951-405a-85c2-03819d5b1512","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"67aee3ce-0b0c-48ee-9822-ff020ecab06d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C2VLfQLaVdwGakzzh2eURP","type":"tool_result","content":"07LEE/gs-object-extraction stars 2 license Apache-2.0 updated 2026-10-11T12:32:05Z lang Python\nExtract objects from 3D Gaussian Splatting scenes and export them as standalone PLY files.\n# 3D Gaussian Splatting Object Extraction\nExtract an object from a trained 3D Gaussian Splatting scene and export it as a standalone PLY. Open the scene in the viewer, click the object from a few angles, and SAM2\n![A scene, and the object extracted from it on white and on black, turning together](docs/images/scene-and-object.webp)\n## Requirements\n- A CUDA GPU, Python 3.10–3.12 and the CUDA Toolkit.\n- A scene already trained with [Graphdeco 3DGS](https://github.com/graphdeco-inria/gaussian-splatting), opened from its `point_cloud.ply`. Training is out of scope.\n## Installation\nFrom the repository root, install PyTorch for your CUDA version (the index URL is for CUDA 12.8), then the tool:\n```bash\npython3 -m venv .venv-gpu\nsource .venv-gpu/bin/activate\npip install --upgrade pip setuptools wheel\npip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128\nSAM2_BUILD_CUDA=0 pip install --no-build-isolation -r requirements.txt\npip install --no-deps -e .\n```\nThe SAM2 checkpoint (about 300 MB) downloads on first use into `~/.cache/gs-object-extraction/checkpoints/`. gsplat compiles its CUDA kernels the first time a scene is op\n## Usage\n```bash\ngs-object-extraction-gui [scene.ply]\n```\n1. **Mark views.** Press **S**, click the object, and SAM2 overlays a mask (right-click what it wrongly includes). **Enter** or **Space** adds the view. Mark about 16 vie\n2. **Extract.** **Ctrl+E**.\n3. **Clean up.** In the object preview, press **S** to select strays by box or click, **X** removes them, **Ctrl+Z** undoes. *Refine* makes the object stand solid; *Rever\n4. **Export.** **Ctrl+Shift+S**.\nThe icons in the top right of the view toggle: Gaussians as blue points, object or scene, white or black background, and a box round the kept Gaussians with its size.\n### Controls\nThe camera moves as in Isaac Sim.\n| Input | Action |\n| --- | --- |\n| Alt + left drag / middle drag / right drag | Orbit / pan / look around |\n| Right drag held + W A S D, Q E | Fly: forward, left, back, right, down, up (Shift: faster; the arrows and Page Up / Down work too) |\n| Alt + right drag, wheel | Zoom |\n| Double-click | Rotation centre under the cursor |\n| S, Enter or Space, Backspace, Esc | Select mode, add view, undo point, clear points or selection |\n| Shift, Ctrl while selecting | Add to, take away from the selection |\n| Ctrl+E, Ctrl+Shift+S | Extract, export |\n### Tuning\nUnder *Advanced* in the *Object* panel:\n- **Off-mask limit**: lower drops more stray Gaussians but thins edges. Extract again after changing it.\n- **Edge trim**: pulls in Gaussians reaching past the masks; `1.00` leaves them.\nSurfaces missing from the source scene cannot be recovered: an object photographed from one side stays hollow on the other.\n## License\n[Apache-2.0](LICENSE). [Third-party licenses](third_party/README.md).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5a51a8e6-a59e-40c1-b5d2-0847a96b87b0","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:29:56.838Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"07LEE/gs-object-extraction stars 2 license Apache-2.0 updated 2026-10-11T12:32:05Z lang Python\nExtract objects from 3D Gaussian Splatting scenes and export them as standalone PLY files.\n# 3D Gaussian Splatting Object Extraction\nExtract an object from a trained 3D Gaussian Splatting scene and export it as a standalone PLY. Open the scene in the viewer, click the object from a few angles, and SAM2\n![A scene, and the object extracted from it on white and on black, turning together](docs/images/scene-and-object.webp)\n## Requirements\n- A CUDA GPU, Python 3.10–3.12 and the CUDA Toolkit.\n- A scene already trained with [Graphdeco 3DGS](https://github.com/graphdeco-inria/gaussian-splatting), opened from its `point_cloud.ply`. Training is out of scope.\n## Installation\nFrom the repository root, install PyTorch for your CUDA version (the index URL is for CUDA 12.8), then the tool:\n```bash\npython3 -m venv .venv-gpu\nsource .venv-gpu/bin/activate\npip install --upgrade pip setuptools wheel\npip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128\nSAM2_BUILD_CUDA=0 pip install --no-build-isolation -r requirements.txt\npip install --no-deps -e .\n```\nThe SAM2 checkpoint (about 300 MB) downloads on first use into `~/.cache/gs-object-extraction/checkpoints/`. gsplat compiles its CUDA kernels the first time a scene is op\n## Usage\n```bash\ngs-object-extraction-gui [scene.ply]\n```\n1. **Mark views.** Press **S**, click the object, and SAM2 overlays a mask (right-click what it wrongly includes). **Enter** or **Space** adds the view. Mark about 16 vie\n2. **Extract.** **Ctrl+E**.\n3. **Clean up.** In the object preview, press **S** to select strays by box or click, **X** removes them, **Ctrl+Z** undoes. *Refine* makes the object stand solid; *Rever\n4. **Export.** **Ctrl+Shift+S**.\nThe icons in the top right of the view toggle: Gaussians as blue points, object or scene, white or black background, and a box round the kept Gaussians with its size.\n### Controls\nThe camera moves as in Isaac Sim.\n| Input | Action |\n| --- | --- |\n| Alt + left drag / middle drag / right drag | Orbit / pan / look around |\n| Right drag held + W A S D, Q E | Fly: forward, left, back, right, down, up (Shift: faster; the arrows and Page Up / Down work too) |\n| Alt + right drag, wheel | Zoom |\n| Double-click | Rotation centre under the cursor |\n| S, Enter or Space, Backspace, Esc | Select mode, add view, undo point, clear points or selection |\n| Shift, Ctrl while selecting | Add to, take away from the selection |\n| Ctrl+E, Ctrl+Shift+S | Extract, export |\n### Tuning\nUnder *Advanced* in the *Object* panel:\n- **Off-mask limit**: lower drops more stray Gaussians but thins edges. Extract again after changing it.\n- **Edge trim**: pulls in Gaussians reaching past the masks; `1.00` leaves them.\nSurfaces missing from the source scene cannot be recovered: an object photographed from one side stays hollow on the other.\n## License\n[Apache-2.0](LICENSE). [Third-party licenses](third_party/README.md).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"dd4f81bc-6c96-47c5-a1de-ef479aed4db4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","branch":"viktor/usage-update","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":null,"remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Sairanyx/Newbies","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4c5c4aec-6951-405a-85c2-03819d5b1512","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/usage-update","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
