{"parentUuid":"5c7a12fc-6d83-4181-b244-f1b30281263c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoVa7QfAN6xFq7vxnFS6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**No, not for the next step. We only need the 5090 if the cuts we already have aren't good enough.** All 59 movable objects can already be dragged, just as outlines. The question is how many move as the real scan, and that has three levels:\n\n| Approach | Needs a GPU? | Quality so far |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Saved mask cuts:** `members.npz` has cuts for 54 objects and is already in the Release | No, `make pieces` runs on CPU | Mixed: only 3 of the 25 I checked looked clean |\n| **Box cuts:** everything in the object's box | No, CPU | Good for free-standing objects like the roll cage, but it takes neighbours along |\n| **Interactive cuts:** `gs-object-extraction` with SAM2 | **Yes**, a CUDA GPU | Unknown, but probably the best for tricky objects |\n\nThe mask cuts can't be regenerated or improved, because that needs the masks on Roihu, which is closed. Re-rendering and running SAM on the 5090 would be the only way to redo them, and I wouldn't set that up now.\n\n**You do need a real GPU to check the results by eye** in the viewer, since it runs at about 1 fps in software here. But any teammate's laptop with a decent graphics card should do for that, so it doesn't have to be the 5090.\n\n## What I'd do\n1. **Pick 8–10 large, free-standing objects** that would read well in the demo, such as carts and chairs. I can shortlist them from the object list and the crop sheet, without a GPU.\n2. **Cut each both ways on CPU**, box and mask, and keep whichever looks better. Trying one is just `make pieces PIECES_OBJECTS=\"...\" PIECES_BOX=\"...\"`.\n3. **Have someone with a GPU check them** in the viewer, for a minute or two each.\n4. **Only use the 5090 tool** on the objects that still look bad and matter for the demo.\n\nObjects in piles or tangles will likely stay as outlines, whichever method we use. Moving something also reveals a patched floor and possibly a marked wall behind it, and those limits don't go away with a bigger GPU.\n\n**I wouldn't chase all 59.** A handful of clean objects show the feature better than dozens of smeared ones, and the rehearsal and plan view are worth more of your time.\n\nWant me to make that shortlist? I can do it alongside the plan view, and neither needs the 5090. PR #24 (usage guide) is also still waiting for your OK to merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1852,"cache_read_input_tokens":892899,"output_tokens":1322,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":492},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1852,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1322,"cache_read_input_tokens":892899,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1852},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9dd598ef-8915-483f-8864-c37012b71631","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoVa6gGN7n9tokFbViuF","requestRef":"41e4f66d-b33e-4bd7-bb02-654aee20b85c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6504f35-8207-4be4-989d-6f3e0f0f35d3","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:32:06.596Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/usage-update","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
