{"parentUuid":"95c2979d-e96b-4bb7-bb56-1eb3b694a3ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoVhaPaz33JA2rvMYGqs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":894751,"output_tokens":1712,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":669},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1350,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1712,"cache_read_input_tokens":894751,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1350,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1350},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7543,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"e24957e6-09d3-4017-bf71-2ec7000e75a9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgoVhZeg6fkPmiDwXQvFD","requestRef":"1547418d-5102-458f-9d74-ec798555c496","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e46701e-8ffe-4a73-89fc-ff0296797da9","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:33:41.268Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/usage-update","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
{"parentUuid":"4e46701e-8ffe-4a73-89fc-ff0296797da9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoVhaPaz33JA2rvMYGqs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Use the 5090 and the laptops. I wouldn't add cloud compute.** Almost everything left runs on one or the other.\n\n| Work | Where it runs |\n|---|---|\n| Cutting objects (`make pieces`), plan view, drafting docs | Laptop, CPU only |\n| Checking cuts by eye | **Laptop browser**, on a light scene |\n| Rehearsal, Qwen copilot test | 5090 |\n| Interactive object extraction (SAM2) | 5090, if we try it |\n| Precision sample crops | 5090, a short job |\n\n## An important thing about the viewer\n**The viewer renders on whichever device opens it, not on the server.** `make web` only serves files, and the splats are drawn by the browser's own GPU. That has three consequences:\n- **Laptops can probably check cuts.** My 1 fps was headless software rendering. A laptop's built-in GPU should do better with `light_400k` and `?res=0.5`, though no one has tried it yet. It's a quick test: run `make web` on a laptop and see.\n- **The tablet draws everything itself.** The 5090 doesn't help its frame rate, only the API and Qwen. So the tablet test matters as much as the 5090 rehearsal, and it needs a light scene.\n- **The full scene only looks its best on a screen connected to the 5090,** so consider that for the recorded video. Laptops and tablets will show a lighter version.\n\n## Why not cloud\n- **Valmet's data:** our pitch is that plant data stays on site. Uploading their scan and video to a commercial cloud needs their OK first, and a project rule keeps Valmet's data out of places it shouldn't be.\n- **Setup time:** a new machine needs drivers, environments and data, which could take hours we don't have, and it replaces work the 5090 can already do.\n- **LUMI is the only alternative I'd consider,** since it answered on SSH earlier and `AGENTS.md` lists it. But its GPUs are AMD, so gsplat and the rest would need porting, and I don't know if your project access works. I wouldn't start there.\n\n## The 5090 is now the bottleneck\nSince it's shared and it's our only GPU, I'd book time on it in this order:\n1. **Rehearsal** (Viktor and Eduard): first, because it may uncover problems.\n2. **Qwen copilot test:** runs in minutes, and I'd need to write the questions first.\n3. **Precision sample crops:** a short job. I can write the script now, and Sasha scores the results.\n4. **SAM2 extraction** (Sasha): last, since it's optional and needs someone at the machine.\n\nCheck `nvidia-smi` before starting anything, and remember Qwen alone takes about 19.5 GB of its memory.\n\n## What I can do from here, without the 5090\n- Build the plan view\n- Shortlist and cut 8–10 candidate objects, for someone to check on a laptop\n- Write the 60-question copilot test and the precision crop script, ready to run on the 5090\n- Draft the README, technical note and slide numbers\n\nShould I start on those, in that order? And is the 5090 free for a rehearsal now?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":894751,"output_tokens":1712,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":669},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1350,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1712,"cache_read_input_tokens":894751,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1350,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1350},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e24957e6-09d3-4017-bf71-2ec7000e75a9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgoVhZeg6fkPmiDwXQvFD","requestRef":"1547418d-5102-458f-9d74-ec798555c496","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6e9ca355-b297-4971-9959-475b8478a360","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:33:52.607Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","sessionId":"6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"viktor/usage-update","slug":"vast-jumping-lobster"}
