{"parentUuid":"00567af0-7126-4b36-a911-4b7f9cdc3e22","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"02e34832-47b7-4b9e-aefa-152f431005be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QxrALpee6sjBcY8NPBFq6P","type":"tool_result","content":"viktor/usage-update\nar viktor-trilar 2852378 Nov  7 11:11 web/vendor/spark/s\nSplatEdit: 6\nSplatEditSdf: 3\nSplatEditSdfType: 1\nSplatEditRgbaBlendMode: 1\nSplatModifier: 1\n7605:\t\tif (super({ update: (e) => this.update(e) }), this.isInitialized = !1, this.recolor = new e.Color(1, 1, 1), this.\n7794:\t\tlet m = this.editable ? (this.edits ?? []).concat(c) : [];\n7795:\t\tthis.editable && !this.edits && this.traverseVisible((e) => {\n---\nflorentPoux/3d-data-materials stars 68 license MIT updated 2026-10-29T09:43:39Z lang Python | Runnable Python behind my 3D data science tutorials. Point clouds, LiDAR, Gaussian splatting, meshing and spatial AI.\ndir .github\nfile .gitignore\ndir 3d-models-from-images\ndir 3d-scene-labeling-gui\nfile CITATION.cff\nfile DATA_LICENSE.md\nfile LICENSE\nfile README.md\ndir assets\ndir evacuation-distance-map\ndir gaussian-splat-to-mesh\ndir lidar-ground-to-dtm\ndir open-vocabulary-3d-semantics\ndir scan-to-floor-plan-dxf\ndir wall-thickness-to-ifc\ndir wheelchair-accessibility-audit\n3D Data Materials\n  The runnable code behind every 3D data science tutorial I publish.\n  Point clouds, LiDAR, Gaussian splatting, meshing and spatial AI, in Python you can read.\n  Datasets ·\n  Tutorials ·\n  The book · Medium ·\n  About\n---\n## What this is\nEvery tutorial I write ships with a script that actually runs. This repository is\nwhere those scripts live, one folder per article, each one self-contained and\ncommented for reading rather than for cleverness.\nNo framework, no package to install from here, no abstraction layer between you\nand the geometry. Each folder is a script you can open, read top to bottom and\nrun, or a pointer to the repository where that script already lives.\nThe datasets are separate, because a 20 MB point cloud does not belong in git\nhistory. Each kit's page on learngeodata.eu hands you the scene the script was\nwritten against, plus the finished output so you can check your result against\nmine.\n## The kits\n### [Walking distance to the nearest exit, from a scan](./evacuation-distance-map)\nOne multi-source Dijkstra from the exits over a 16-neighbour grid, routes by descent, dead-end corridors from graph bridges, and a what-if for every blocked door. CPU onl\n- Code: [`evacuation-distance-map/`](./evacuation-distance-map)\n- Data: [learngeodata.eu/materials/evacuation-distance-map/](https://learngeodata.eu/materials/evacuation-distance-map/)\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/wall_thickness_to_ifc.py\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/README.md\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/run.bat\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/visualize.py\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/check_determinism.py","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"96829eec-6637-4d6f-8eb2-8b0a9ec07cd9","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:39:13.568Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"viktor/usage-update\nar viktor-trilar 2852378 Nov  7 11:11 web/vendor/spark/s\nSplatEdit: 6\nSplatEditSdf: 3\nSplatEditSdfType: 1\nSplatEditRgbaBlendMode: 1\nSplatModifier: 1\n7605:\t\tif (super({ update: (e) => this.update(e) }), this.isInitialized = !1, this.recolor = new e.Color(1, 1, 1), this.\n7794:\t\tlet m = this.editable ? (this.edits ?? []).concat(c) : [];\n7795:\t\tthis.editable && !this.edits && this.traverseVisible((e) => {\n---\nflorentPoux/3d-data-materials stars 68 license MIT updated 2026-10-29T09:43:39Z lang Python | Runnable Python behind my 3D data science tutorials. Point clouds, LiDAR, Gaussian splatting, meshing and spatial AI.\ndir .github\nfile .gitignore\ndir 3d-models-from-images\ndir 3d-scene-labeling-gui\nfile CITATION.cff\nfile DATA_LICENSE.md\nfile LICENSE\nfile README.md\ndir assets\ndir evacuation-distance-map\ndir gaussian-splat-to-mesh\ndir lidar-ground-to-dtm\ndir open-vocabulary-3d-semantics\ndir scan-to-floor-plan-dxf\ndir wall-thickness-to-ifc\ndir wheelchair-accessibility-audit\n3D Data Materials\n  The runnable code behind every 3D data science tutorial I publish.\n  Point clouds, LiDAR, Gaussian splatting, meshing and spatial AI, in Python you can read.\n  Datasets ·\n  Tutorials ·\n  The book · Medium ·\n  About\n---\n## What this is\nEvery tutorial I write ships with a script that actually runs. This repository is\nwhere those scripts live, one folder per article, each one self-contained and\ncommented for reading rather than for cleverness.\nNo framework, no package to install from here, no abstraction layer between you\nand the geometry. Each folder is a script you can open, read top to bottom and\nrun, or a pointer to the repository where that script already lives.\nThe datasets are separate, because a 20 MB point cloud does not belong in git\nhistory. Each kit's page on learngeodata.eu hands you the scene the script was\nwritten against, plus the finished output so you can check your result against\nmine.\n## The kits\n### [Walking distance to the nearest exit, from a scan](./evacuation-distance-map)\nOne multi-source Dijkstra from the exits over a 16-neighbour grid, routes by descent, dead-end corridors from graph bridges, and a what-if for every blocked door. CPU onl\n- Code: [`evacuation-distance-map/`](./evacuation-distance-map)\n- Data: [learngeodata.eu/materials/evacuation-distance-map/](https://learngeodata.eu/materials/evacuation-distance-map/)\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/wall_thickness_to_ifc.py\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/README.md\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/run.bat\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/visualize.py\nwall-thickness-to-ifc/check_determinism.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e2183676-bb8a-4450-9273-deb2626a16cf","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","root":"/home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies","branch":"viktor/usage-update","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"cou